{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them","id":1485320,"title":"Anarch domains: why official supplements ignore them?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-29T17:12:36-07:00","id":1485320,"title":"Anarch domains: why official supplements ignore them?","content":"The title, basically: why do you think we never got a decently flashed out anarch domain? In the years we got loads of Camarilla ones, a few Sabbat ones and even one Autarkis one (Cairo). All we got for Anarchs are contested domains (the former Free State basically) and, recently, a shortt write up for Indianapolis (which is more a Setite city than an Anarch one). Why do you think game designers are so reluctant writing a supplement for a full Anarch domain?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Also: which city would be good to represent an Anarch domain?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 06-29-2022, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T17:38:54-07:00","id":1485323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them#post1485320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The title, basically: why do you think we never got a decently flashed out anarch domain? In the years we got loads of Camarilla ones, a few Sabbat ones and even one Autarkis one (Cairo). All we got for Anarchs are contested domains (the former Free State basically) and, recently, a shortt write up for Indianapolis (which is more a Setite city than an Anarch one). Why do you think game designers are so reluctant writing a supplement for a full Anarch domain?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Also: which city would be good to represent an Anarch domain?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Simply put, because the original LA by Night ruined Anarch domains and the anarch cause for everyone for decades until V20 came up to remember the time when anarchs, misguided or not were the heroes and antiheroes of the game. Bloodlines and the youtube series have done much to salvage things since, but the original LA by Night book was that toxic for VtM and the anarchs as a whole.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, it's a proccess, we are seeing the uphill movement to reverse damages done in the mid to late 2nd edition and whole of Revised era, that was directed by Achilli, a guy who hated anarchs and very much missed their point even before that. While dealing with V5's own baggage of whole new drama and polemics along the way might be said.<br /> <br /> Honestly, we should count ourselves lucky for anarchs getting more love than they have had since the 90s with all the ups &amp; downs of the last edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-29-2022, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T17:52:25-07:00","id":1485324,"title":"","content":"Why was LA by Night so bad? I\u2019ve never read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T18:13:34-07:00","id":1485326,"title":"","content":"I think part of it may be that Anarch domains are so far from the D&amp;D model of supplements that writers really don't know how to construct them. Camarilla is pretty simple: there's a Prince, he's got some people who want his job, and he's got some masquerade problems or military problems he can hire the players to fix. The players socialize at some fancy parties to get the job, do some detective work that may reveal the original enemy they were hired to find, or may reveal some dirty political machinations, and they kick some ass here and there. It's not really all THAT different from a D&amp;D game, except that keeping things secret from the public is important, and there's angsting about your humanity.<br /> <br /> Now let's look at an Anarch &quot;domain&quot;. There's a bunch of gangs. They squabble openly for territory, only joining forces when there's an invasion by the Sabbat or Camarilla. There's nothing much to do in an Anarch domain except prepare your haven for the next territorial gang squabble or Sabbat/Cammy invasion.<br /> <br /> I really don't get the appeal of Anarchs. There's none of the layers of political mystery that the Camarilla offers. There's none of the engrossing feel of trying to roleplay dedication to, and advancement on, a Path of Enlightenment that the Sabbat gives, which gives the players personal storyhooks beyond the ST's plot, all while trying to root out Infernalism, or dealing with demagoguery by Path leaders whose appeal to the masses greatly outstrips their military competence.(I'm looking at you Cathari, you useless demagogues turning the Sabbat into perverts with no territory to call home by appealing to the masses of shovelheads.)<br /> <br /> There's just, we're free, but those guys over there want to take it from us, so let's prepare a lot and then sit around until they invade. Maybe fight the gang next door that we'll have to ally with during the next invasion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 06-29-2022, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T20:56:19-07:00","id":1485330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485324#post1485324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why was LA by Night so bad? I\u2019ve never read it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of the By Night books other than Chicago By Night, it was typical - meaning it was rather mediocre. It wasn't &quot;awful&quot;. Just useless. <br /> <br /> The problem is that this was supposed to be THE showcase for the Anarchs. So many people went &quot;This is all there is?&quot; and moved on. And unlike the Camarilla, you couldn't say &quot;This is just one domain, I can set my game in some other domain&quot; and let your imagination go wild. Instead, the Los Angeles area was basically it unless you wanted to set it in Madison, Wisconsin. So the LA Free State REALLY needed to sell itself as a great setting.<br /> <br /> The vampire NPCs were mainly generic and uninteresting. It did not take advantage of many of the interesting things about the Los Angeles area, for example anything dealing with Hollywood is conspicuously absent except for a few immaterial mentions. It defined ALL the conflict within the Anarch Free States as gang warfare which was boring. It did not provide any meaningful political or personality differences between the various factions of Anarchs. And it introduced yet ANOTHER Methusaleh (in generation if not in age) as being behind most things, which was already a hack trope by the time the sourcebook came out.<br /> <br /> There's a few interesting NPCs to be sure, but many of those were already introduced in the Anarch Cookbook or elsewhere. So it really didn't add much. It was just a waste of space.<br /> <br /> Most people armed with a 3L bottle of Jolt, and DVDs of LA Confidential, the Player, Chinatown, Falling Down, Heat, and Boyz n the Hood for an all night movie marathon can probably brainstorm much more interesting aspects for a vampire chronicle set in LA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T21:21:15-07:00","id":1485332,"title":"","content":"I don't think LA by Night was so bad (not the worse definitely) and I also disagree there aren't interesting plot hooks in an Anarch domain. I must add that I am a RL anarchist, so the politics of Anarchy is something that deeply interests me.<br /> My players are actually in LA by Night setting right now, LA 1991. They are from Chicago and doing a job for Kevin Jackson, trying to close a deal to get the Bloods, who are just three Ventrue Neonates but have a lot of mortal power, recognised as a full Barony, obviously against the well established Crips. <br /> Now, the actual job can be accomplished in a lot of different ways. They can try to convince enough people to support their claim; for this route I am presenting them different types of Anarchs that can be convinced, bribed or both to give them support; some are established barons, some leaders of roaming biker gangs, some are heroes of the revolution, some are idealistic, some pragmatic, most something in between. There is also an investigation route, in which they can try to uncover some dirty secrets of the Crips and expose them (or threaten to do so); they may need to work with some Nosferatu in order to accomplish that. There are probably some other things I haven't thought about but my players will. And there is a betrayal that the PC's may or not discover before it's too late.<br /> My point is that you can run interesting stories with interesting themes in Anarch domains... You just need to stop seeing them as a one dimensional lot and look at them as different people with different goals, ideas and outlooks in unlife. There are good guys (or least they are trying), there are demagogues and blind fanatics. The main difference with a Camarilla or a Sabbat domain is how conflict between them is resolved (and no, it doesn't necessarily involve just fighting for turf with guns and katanas)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T23:04:40-07:00","id":1485335,"title":"","content":"I did a RPG.net review of LA by Night and basically my problem with the book was the following points:<br /> <br /> 1. The Anarchs are exposed as basically identical to the Camarilla. Instead of Princes, you have Barons, and they enforce their territory with gangs that kill anyone who feeds in their territory that they don't like (or just beats them up if they're nice). In short, the Anarchs look like they have absolutely no interest in &quot;reforming&quot; Kindred society, they just hate that they're not in charge.<br /> <br /> 2. The game only shows variations on the same archetypes of Brujah, Caitiff, and other thugs with a few memorable characters like Louis Fortier, Salvador, and Jeremy MacNeil. The fact this is the city of LOS ANGELES and they don't have anyone in Hollywood but a Bela Lugosi impersonator is a massive waste.<br /> <br /> 3. The Anarchs are constantly fighting each other and killing each other, which is another sign that they're not a viable alternative to the Camarilla. It even makes the Camarilla look better because you're unlikely to be randomly murdered in their territory.<br /> <br /> 4. The glorification of gang culture came off as particularly poor taste given the Crack Epidemic and RL murders happening in LA at the time with hundreds of young men and women gunned down that traumatized a generation. Here, the Crips and the Bloods are vampires versus vampire hunters, which is just tasteless. Worse, they cite <i>Boyz in the Hood</i>, which is about the tragedy of the situation.<br /> <br /> 5. Even the Methusaleh controlling LA, the second largest city in the United States, is a fifteen year old boy that get crushes on handsome charismatic warrior Kindred. It doesn't even have the dignity of a real mastermind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485326#post1485326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't get the appeal of Anarchs. There's none of the layers of political mystery that the Camarilla offers. There's none of the engrossing feel of trying to roleplay dedication to, and advancement on, a Path of Enlightenment that the Sabbat gives, which gives the players personal storyhooks beyond the ST's plot, all while trying to root out Infernalism, or dealing with demagoguery by Path leaders whose appeal to the masses greatly outstrips their military competence.(I'm looking at you Cathari, you useless demagogues turning the Sabbat into perverts with no territory to call home by appealing to the masses of shovelheads.)<br /> <br /> There's just, we're free, but those guys over there want to take it from us, so let's prepare a lot and then sit around until they invade. Maybe fight the gang next door that we'll have to ally with during the next invasion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Anarchs best work in a Camarilla city as they're basically an essential part of doing what I consider to be a &quot;classic&quot; Vampire: The Masquerade game. The Anarchs serve as one of the factions in a city against the Prince and Elders. They've got their own intrigues, though, and power plays.<br /> <br /> The first Anarch, Juggler, is just as manipulative and scheming as the first Camarilla Prince, Modius. However, Juggler talks a good game of freedom and liberty but he just uses Neonates as cannon fodder for his own ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T23:05:09-07:00","id":1485336,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that's the refutation of the previous posts you think it is. It's basically the narrative version of the Rule Zero Fallacy. &quot;Anarchs are great if you put in all the time and effort into making them fun that the books didn't do,&quot; means the Anarchs aren't well described in the books for eliciting good stories that don't involve a lot of real world knowledge of various topics and copious research.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T00:06:55-07:00","id":1485339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485336#post1485336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that's the refutation of the previous posts you think it is. It's basically the narrative version of the Rule Zero Fallacy. &amp;quot;Anarchs are great if you put in all the time and effort into making them fun that the books didn't do,&amp;quot; means the Anarchs aren't well described in the books for eliciting good stories that don't involve a lot of real world knowledge of various topics and copious research.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I never thought I was refuting any previous posts. Actually, you are probably right and most published material authors didn't even have a clue about what anarchism really is. What I wanted to change was the vision that most people have of the Anarchs precisely BECAUSE OF the published books (Chicago by Night 1st edition being the great exception)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T01:00:19-07:00","id":1485341,"title":"","content":"In fairness, I don't think the writers need to know the details of the human political philosophy called anarchism, because that simply isn't what the vampire movement is about. To start with, vampires are predators. They don't need money, they need hunting territory, so human economic systems mean very little to them. They just don't want older vampires telling them where to hunt or punishing them for masquerade breaches and such things. By and large they consider the masquerade to be common sense, and masquerade breachers to be a self-fixing problem. In other words, the breachers will either quickly learn to be more careful, in which case punishing them is just killing someone who meant no harm and has learned his lesson, or hunters will give them a final Darwin award in the form of a stake and a blade, no need for a dictatorial system as you can let nature take its course.<br /> <br /> And that's about all the Anarchs agree on. Some may hold to idealistic notions, albeit with very little ability to institute them, both because the other Anarchs are just as free to ignore them as they are to ignore everyone else, and also because vampire economics are so wildly different from human economics that it doesn't translate.<br /> <br /> Some simply want the personal freedom to lobotomize a bunch of humans and live on a plantation with their ghouled slaves and lobotomized herd with no Prince telling them that such a large and blatantly monstrous operation is a masquerade breach waiting to happen. Those guys are just as much anarchs as any idealist.<br /> <br /> Ultimately vampire needs mean any society they form is going to be closer to various one-resource dictatorships than any more egalitarian society. If all that matters is oil, then everyone is gong to fight over control of the oil, and whoever wins is going to be the dictator, right up until another group overthrows them and takes control over the oil and the wealth it provides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 06-30-2022, 04:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T01:30:39-07:00","id":1485342,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day, Vampire society is unfair. Old, lower generation vampires will simply be more powerful than younger, higher generation vampires. The oldest and lowest generation vampire will end up in charge of city. If he or she doesn't want to bother with ruling directly, then someone else might be allowed to rule. But that &quot;puppet' Prince had better do what the older and more powerful vampire wants and if they don't they're going to be replaced ands the oldest, lowest generation vampire will inevitably be the secret ruler behind the throne. <br /> <br /> The Prince system sucks but it's kind of inevitable and this was the biggest problem that the writers ran into. They couldn't really come up with new, functional political systems for the Anarchs that wouldn't implode under the weight of older, more powerful vampires. You could have a system with something like elections, but once you toss in Disciplines like Presence and Dominate, how meaningful are those elections? So Anarchs inevitably end up with a pretty similar society to the Camarilla: a system in which the oldest, lowest generation vampire is the one calling the shots, just with the labels changed. But it doesn't matter if you call that vampire Prince or Baron or Boss or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T01:37:06-07:00","id":1485343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485335#post1485335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Anarchs best work in a Camarilla city as they're basically an essential part of doing what I consider to be a &quot;classic&quot; Vampire: The Masquerade game. The Anarchs serve as one of the factions in a city against the Prince and Elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man, given our (seeming) disagreements about the role of the anarchs and the Camarilla in the past, it's fun to read this. I agree with the above 100%, and this is more or less all I've ever meant when I say that &quot;the anarchs are a faction within the Camarilla.&quot; It doesn't mean that the anarchs should be portrayed as ineffective squabblers who talk a big game about freedom but kowtow to the Camarilla party line whenever push comes to shove. It just means that the anarchs work best as the part of the Camarilla that is aggressively (sometimes violently) pushing for change.<br /> <br /> The original game defined the Camarilla as an idea that covered more or less the entirety of acceptable vampire society -- from the Elders at the top to the various malcontents in the gutter. I don't think the V5 approach of narrowing down the concept of the Camarilla into <i>just</i> the faction for princes and snooty Elders is doing the setting any favors. When both the Camarilla and the Sabbat are reduced to outside forces trying to move in on anarch territory in the style of <i>Vampire: The Masquerade \u2013 Bloodlines</i>, but the game adamantly refuses to detail how to make the anarchs playable whenever outside forces are <i>not</i> trying to move in on their territory, there's a gaping void where the center of the game should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T03:20:24-07:00","id":1485348,"title":"","content":"The Anarchs just don't make sense as a main sect. They work better as small subset within the main sects; the main sects being the Camarilla and the Sabbat. The moment the Anarchs become a main sect, they also become The Man. The Man has to solve nitty-gritty problems that require organization and hierarchy and once you have organization and hierarchy, you're going to have the oldest and most powerful corrupting it.<br /> <br /> In fact it feels kind of silly that the Anarchs could ever have a major military victory over the Camarilla or the Sabbat. The Sabbat and Cammies have actual military leaders who can expect large forces to obey them in an organized fashion. By rights, they should literally roll over the Anarchs. It would be like the January 6th mob trying to defend territory against an actual organized conquering army. The moment they try to prevent that by truly organizing their own army, they've stopped being Anarchs and might as well not bother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T04:15:20-07:00","id":1485351,"title":"","content":"So many posts here reflect how little people know about anarchism as a political philosophy....<br /> 1. It doesn't really matter if would be anarchists need money or hunting grounds. Anarchism is a political philosophy and its main point is the abolition of hierarchy. Any way to organise the resources according to this principle is ok.<br /> 2. Anarchism is not dependent on people being equal. There will always be stronger, wiser or cleverer people. Anarchism is based on the WILL to cooperate and not dominate. Can human do It? Can vampires? Well, as someone mentioned in a different posts, vampires are fictional beings and the only definitive truths about them are the stories and themes we want to tell (or play)<br /> 3. Organization and hierarchy are not the same. People can organise very efficiently in non hierarchical ways, and some have even proved effective even for military purposes. So the Anarchs could have their society.<br /> <br /> For a fictional setting with functional anarchist societies I strongly recommend the RPG Eclipse Phase. But that's a game made by developers who actually understood anarchism and not guya who equated it to bikers in leather","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T04:56:07-07:00","id":1485354,"title":"","content":"Its an intrinsic writting problem with the anarchs. They're undeveloped and are only really defined by reactive personal grudges. Even the speeches about freedom come across as pathetic when you pull the thread since they have a total lack of praxis. The problem was aggravated in v5 because of increased emphasis on them.<br /> <br /> They actually worked a lot better in Revised as a dissident element in carmarilla society or holdouts in Sabbat. When they hold actually uncontested territory their complete lack of civic institions and distinct from other sect organization becomes a real problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T04:57:27-07:00","id":1485355,"title":"","content":"Doylist: Because sometimes having all the options causes a lack of direction and confusion; the Camarilla offers a good base to build your city on with just the right amount of boundries to stop you going off the rails; choice and freedom can be a burden on it's own: Look up the &quot;overchoice effect&quot;. Anarchs let players anmd the storyteller play around with paths and encourages them to play weird bloodlines, but that can get in the way of a tightly crafted game with more relatable characters. <br /> <br /> <br /> Watsonian: Because Anarch domains are logically few. Anarchs can't be strongly defined by anything more than &quot;vampire groups opposed to a prince&quot;. In most cases, the quiet majority of &quot;Anarchs&quot; are just Camarilla with a few disagreements. The Vocal minority of Anarchs that rail hard against authority are dysfunctional fools who aren't likely to gain significant holdings. In the rare instances that radicals do gain significant holdings, the surrounding powers will do their best to undermine and disrupt such a rule; a well functioning anarch state is a threat to the concept of princedom, and given the power of Camarilla-in-groups vs the power of the types that can't make it in the Camarilla, it's unsurprising that the anarchs come out on the bottom all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T05:13:18-07:00","id":1485356,"title":"","content":"My guess is that between the SI wiping them out (I'm pretty sure that the anarchs account for the majority of SI kills) and the fact that anarchs are, at their core, a bunch of fucking idiots who are only good at farting out slogans without actually having the competence to manage a domain, most of the &quot;anarch&quot; domains are probably held by former camarilla ancillae that decided to strike on their own and gain more power using the anarchs as easily manipulated cannon fodder so aside from a few, largely cosmetic changes, I would guess that a successful anarch domain wouldn't be that different from a camarilla one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T05:18:43-07:00","id":1485357,"title":"","content":"It could be interesting to see what the writers would do with a new <i>Berlin by Night</i>, given its background.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485351#post1485351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So many posts here reflect how little people know about anarchism as a political philosophy....<br /> 1. It doesn't really matter if would be anarchists need money or hunting grounds. Anarchism is a political philosophy and its main point is the abolition of hierarchy. Any way to organise the resources according to this principle is ok.<br /> 2. Anarchism is not dependent on people being equal. There will always be stronger, wiser or cleverer people. Anarchism is based on the WILL to cooperate and not dominate. Can human do It? Can vampires? Well, as someone mentioned in a different posts, vampires are fictional beings and the only definitive truths about them are the stories and themes we want to tell (or play)<br /> 3. Organization and hierarchy are not the same. People can organise very efficiently in non hierarchical ways, and some have even proved effective even for military purposes. So the Anarchs could have their society.<br /> <br /> For a fictional setting with functional anarchist societies I strongly recommend the RPG Eclipse Phase. But that's a game made by developers who actually understood anarchism and not guya who equated it to bikers in leather</div> </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla fosters antagnonism between characters e.g. the plucky neonates and the draconian prince. Would anarchist Anarchs have equivalent conflicts? I don't know what Eclipse Phase is, but I found this list at the end of a guide and maybe some of these could be translated into a VtM Anarch story:<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;What Are Some Problems an Anarchist Hab Might Face?</b><br /> <br /> Anarchists have some good ideas on how to do things, but no system is perfect. Everyone has flaws and some people will always find ways to exploit loopholes. Here\u2019s a short list of some possibilities:<ul><li>Assholes and sociopaths</li> <li>Informal hierarchies that become entrenched</li> <li>Parasites and slackers</li> <li>Hab-hopping offenders</li> <li>Manipulative people who accumulate social capital and abuse it</li> <li>Cliques</li> <li>Xenophobia</li> <li>Lack of accountability</li> <li>Collective proccesses that become overtly bureaucratic</li> <li>People that game/hack rep networks</li> <li>Factional disputes, infighting, and splits</li> <li>Issues incorporating non-anarchists</li> <li>Rare and scarce resources</li> <li>Sabotage or even outright attacks from hostile factions</li> <li>The spread of misinformation and paranoia</li> <li>Collective discussions bogging down and taking forever&quot;</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T06:33:14-07:00","id":1485364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485357#post1485357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be interesting to see what the writers would do with a new <i>Berlin by Night</i>, given its background.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Camarilla fosters antagnonism between characters e.g. the plucky neonates and the draconian prince. Would anarchist Anarchs have equivalent conflicts? I don't know what Eclipse Phase is, but I found this list at the end of a guide and maybe some of these could be translated into a VtM Anarch story:<br /> <br /> <b>&amp;quot;What Are Some Problems an Anarchist Hab Might Face?</b><br /> <br /> Anarchists have some good ideas on how to do things, but no system is perfect. Everyone has flaws and some people will always find ways to exploit loopholes. Here\u2019s a short list of some possibilities:<ul><li>Assholes and sociopaths</li> <li>Informal hierarchies that become entrenched</li> <li>Parasites and slackers</li> <li>Hab-hopping offenders</li> <li>Manipulative people who accumulate social capital and abuse it</li> <li>Cliques</li> <li>Xenophobia</li> <li>Lack of accountability</li> <li>Collective proccesses that become overtly bureaucratic</li> <li>People that game/hack rep networks</li> <li>Factional disputes, infighting, and splits</li> <li>Issues incorporating non-anarchists</li> <li>Rare and scarce resources</li> <li>Sabotage or even outright attacks from hostile factions</li> <li>The spread of misinformation and paranoia</li> <li>Collective discussions bogging down and taking forever&amp;quot;</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Every anarchist worth their salt understands anarchy is not an utopian state without conflicts or full of perfectly boring and well behaved people. Actually, it can be argued that idealistic view of anarchism is as much anti anarchist propaganda as the view that makes an anarchist society a living hell where everyone is fighting everyone all the time (LA by Night). It's just a different, and hopefully better, way to deal with human nature. <br /> So yes, you can run a lot of different and interesting stories in an Anarch domain. We only need authors that understand the topic at hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T09:56:08-07:00","id":1485387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485364#post1485364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every anarchist worth their salt understands anarchy is not an utopian state without conflicts or full of perfectly boring and well behaved people. Actually, it can be argued that idealistic view of anarchism is as much anti anarchist propaganda as the view that makes an anarchist society a living hell where everyone is fighting everyone all the time (LA by Night). It's just a different, and hopefully better, way to deal with human nature.<br /> So yes, you can run a lot of different and interesting stories in an Anarch domain. We only need authors that understand the topic at hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds very difficult to write about a flawed, but more desirable alternative society. Perhaps this is why some sci-fi productions tend to be so unaspirational: one problem that we don't have is scarier than the problems that we take for granted in real life.<br /> <br /> God knows how we'd get this without the community calling it both woke and reactionary. Maybe it's a matter of presenting Anarchs as villains first, but with redeeming features, like the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T10:00:14-07:00","id":1485388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485351#post1485351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So many posts here reflect how little people know about anarchism as a political philosophy....<br /> 1. It doesn't really matter if would be anarchists need money or hunting grounds. Anarchism is a political philosophy and its main point is the abolition of hierarchy. Any way to organise the resources according to this principle is ok.<br /> 2. Anarchism is not dependent on people being equal. There will always be stronger, wiser or cleverer people. Anarchism is based on the WILL to cooperate and not dominate. Can human do It? Can vampires? Well, as someone mentioned in a different posts, vampires are fictional beings and the only definitive truths about them are the stories and themes we want to tell (or play)<br /> 3. Organization and hierarchy are not the same. People can organise very efficiently in non hierarchical ways, and some have even proved effective even for military purposes. So the Anarchs could have their society.<br /> <br /> For a fictional setting with functional anarchist societies I strongly recommend the RPG Eclipse Phase. But that's a game made by developers who actually understood anarchism and not guya who equated it to bikers in leather</div> </div> </div> </div>This is because Anarchs are related to the Anarchy as a British period (meaning &quot;without rule&quot;) of history and predates anarchism (small a) as a philosophy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T12:23:42-07:00","id":1485403,"title":"","content":"Well. I think Anarchs should be, by V5, pretty much the most common or populous; simply because kind of every vampire is Embraced in &quot;&quot;Anarch&quot;&quot;, especially since Camarilla no longer takes every single vamp as their own. The difference between autarkis, independent and anarch sometimes eludes me, but I assume when someone calls you Anarch it is by the political movement in the Kindred world, not of this social state your in, like autarkis I think is kind of just anti-sect or simply an independent body. Either way, I agree we don't get more than bits of any Anarch night by night situation, and those we get aren't good.<br /> <br /> Even though V5s Anarchs book disappoints by lack of tangible material it does show that the &quot;sect&quot; is like a hot pot of spices and flavors. It is not that they don't have rules or societies , they simply are unique in each city and region. We could call the Old Clan Tzimisce domains of Romania de facto Anarchs in a way. And there are cities where vampiric society is almost a Sabbat vampirism-idolatry (there is a chapter in the Anarch book about a city where regularly Kindred gather and beat the shit out of each other in games, just to celebrate immortality). <br /> <br /> But most especially, I would say it kind of is a playground. Problem is the company isn't giving us tangible tools and examples, so it is lackluster to say the least. Most of all I think we would see either a commune-type of city, a gang-turf city, a dictatorial city, or a cultful city. The latter I think is one of the most interesting, cuz you can have a Bahari cult wrestling with the Church of Set, only for the Cult of Mithras come in avidly, and then Packs of Nodist arrive to put gasoline into the flames!! <br /> While gang-turfs I believe are what we mostly imagine. With bids of power by self-proclaimed Barons, which are more like crime lords. If it is all well in good, it could actually become a mafia structure, with &quot;families&quot; or coteries having right or duty to take care of areas of the city. That would be kind of like a commune where every Anarch tries to do its part for the well-being of the city's Kindred. It's just a different society, not anti-society. <br /> <br /> I believe Anarch domains are ones you should take every crazy distopic, utopic, zany, fantastical or crazy idea and put it to practice. Hell, you could have a crazy Anarch domain where everyone behaves as if part of a Chivalric Order that has existed since the Dark Ages as a Military Order of Knights of the Bitter Ashes. One Anarch city could have a School of some sort where fledlings spend a couple of years learning to be Kindred. There is also one example in the Anarch book where Kindred live in an awesome and crazy resort in the mountains where to stay there you got to spent millions of bucks. <br /> <br /> In summary there is a lot of interesting directions, but goddamn, we have no material whatsoever. I love Hecata and cults, and I'm happy for Cult of the Blood Gods, but we needed that much material and chronicles just for the Anarch sect too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T12:46:15-07:00","id":1485407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485403#post1485403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well. I think Anarchs should be, by V5, pretty much the most common or populous; simply because kind of every vampire is Embraced in &quot;&quot;Anarch&quot;&quot;, especially since Camarilla no longer takes every single vamp as their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a hard time getting my head around this because it's really the prince that decides who's an anarch and who isn't. If Princes want a stable rule in a stable city, it's nonsensical to deny Camarilla status to childer with sires of good standing, who sought permission to embrace. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The difference between autarkis, independent and anarch sometimes eludes me. </div> </div> </div>Autark is an old word for independent, just to make matters worse. Independent is a pretty bad word for the FoS/A/Gio, since they're more sects than clans and many belong to camarilla cities and abide by camarilla rules. <br /> <br /> If we go by the game's definitions, an Autark doesn't give a shit about a wider reform or revolution, an Autark is an outlaw that'll be hunted in most cities. An Anarch does belong to group that champions reform or revolution, at least nominally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T13:31:30-07:00","id":1485414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485332#post1485332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think LA by Night was so bad (not the worse definitely) and I also disagree there aren't interesting plot hooks in an Anarch domain. I must add that I am a RL anarchist, so the politics of Anarchy is something that deeply interests me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's important to note that the definition of an Anarch in Vampire has nothing to do with anarchism. It's perfectly fine for an Anarch (capital A) to be an anarchist. But many Anarchs, probably the vast majority, are not. The definition of an Anarch in Vampire is just &quot;a vampire who does not accept the authority of the Inner Circle to govern all vampires, and who is not a member of the Sabbat&quot;. <br /> <br /> (The Independent Clans, in fact, are generally not actually independent in the sense they are free from the Inner Circle. Instead, they had some other arrangement with the Inner Circle that still governed their relationship in some capacity. The Giovanni had the Promise of 1528. The Assamites had the Treaty of Tyre. The Setites didn't have any formal treaty, but were offered membership, had individual &quot;members&quot; of the Camarilla, and kept any of their subversions secret rather than open. Only the Ravnos weren't really regulated, and originally they were just merry wandering vagabonds that the Camarilla could ignore most of the time.)<br /> <br /> An Anarch could be someone who believes in representative or direct democracy. It could be someone who believes in some kind of libertarian utopian. It could be an archconservative vampire who prefers who it was in the Dark Ages BEFORE the Anarch Revolt when Princes could do anything without a Justicar or Conclave interfering. It could be someone who believes there should be a single Lord of the Vampires that all other vampires obey (don't laugh, that's essentially the perspective of the Sabbat with Caine as King and since he's absent our Regent will do, and the Sabbat are supposed to be the original Anarchs). And of course, it could just be criminal thugs who want an excuse/cover for their own crimes. And much of the time, an &quot;Anarch&quot; is just someone the local Prince is crapping on.<br /> <br /> Now in actuality, most Anarchs are concerned with the abuses of the elders and want more freedom for the neonates and those with inferior generation. But there's a variety of ways to handle that issue. The actual view of anarchists are just one faction within that, and probably a small one.<br /> <br /> But it would've been neat to actually have a group of actual vampire anarchists in the Free States, and compare them to other factions equally Anarch, but who want a different political arrangement.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T16:45:02-07:00","id":1485427,"title":"","content":"I don't think Anarchs domains are unfeasible or that Anarchs should only be relegated as a part of the Camarilla. While it's true that there is no such thing as a &quot;standard&quot; anarch domain some &quot;institutions&quot; tend to appear more often than others. The Baron, obviously, but then Emissaries, Sweepers and Chamelons are positions that exist throughout all sorts of Anarch domains. Also having cities that are all the same variation of &quot;the Camarilla runs the place, the Anarchs are rousing rabble in the most rundown neighborhoods but can't achieve much&quot; can only sustain so many stories before becoming stale.<br /> I believe making Anarchs domains could actually be very interesting and a breath of fresh air, actually:<br /> -Anarchs are usually organised in rival gangs (coteries) and the Baron is unlikely to have enough personal power to dominate the political landscape alone (Washington DC is the exception), being more often than not, &quot;primus inter pares&quot; this provides ample material for stories (rivalries, alliances, turf wars...).<br /> -Anarchs can be on the offensive vs the Camarilla which is something hinted but never really explored in VtM. V5 has introduced the notion of Anarchs being capable of toppling even strong Camarilla domains but never bothered to do anything with this lead and it's a waste.<br /> -Anarch stories allow for a different set of themes compared to Camarilla and Sabbat stories, idealism vs reality for one. You may have ideals but what are you willing to do to achieve them? You don't want power (in the beginning at least) but you need power in order to make a change...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T17:10:50-07:00","id":1485429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485355#post1485355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Anarch domains are logically few. Anarchs can't be strongly defined by anything more than &quot;vampire groups opposed to a prince&quot;. In most cases, the quiet majority of &quot;Anarchs&quot; are just Camarilla with a few disagreements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, most Anarchs were really just &quot;Anti-Prince of the city they live in.&quot; If the Prince died or was replaced, those Anarchs would go right back to being regular members of the city's Camarilla. And most Anarchs in one city don't really care too much about Anarchs in another city. They care about getting rid of the Prince of Tulsa, but they don't really care about the Prince of Atlanta or the Anarchs in Atlanta. There are some, a minority, of Anarchs who really are anti-Camarilla, but those guys mostly all went off to California to try and start up the Free State.<br /> <br /> So the Anarchs you find in most cities outside of California are really only Anarchs because they oppose the Prince, not because they want to overthrow the Camarilla or set up their own new political system or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-30-2022, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T19:32:28-07:00","id":1485437,"title":"","content":"<b>Why be an Anarch? I mean, the reason is obvious: feudalism sucks if you're not the king.</b><br /> <br /> Eh,<br /> <br /> My take on the Anarchs is something that's a bit more forgiving than most people. I think most Anarchs are actually quite reasonable in their demands but the problem is that a lot of fans are not taking the time to recognize how fundamentally INSANE the situation is. They're used to &quot;buying in&quot; to the oddities of a RPG so they ignore that almost everyone not born into the Ventrue, Toreador, or Tremere will be inclined to Anarchism.<br /> <br /> Essentially, you awaken to a new world as a vampire and that comes with its ups and downs (to say the least). However, in addition to the horrifying thirst you now possess, you also find out that you are subject to the whims as well as control of a feudal system that no one has been living under for a thousand years. You are also subject to the laws of an organization that will kill you if you break one of their seemingly arbitrary laws.<br /> <br /> Now a lot of this is subject to the interpretation of the ST as well as what sort of Prince you have but if you want an Anarch game then it's not hard to make it seem reasonable to oppose them:<br /> <br /> * &quot;Feed from this mortal, you've violated an Elder's domain.&quot;<br /> * &quot;Feed in this place, you've violated this Elder's domain.&quot;<br /> * &quot;Ditch your mortal identity and give up everything you have [if the Prince feels like it] while some other asshole can go on pretending to be alive.&quot;<br /> * &quot;You can't Embrace your girlfriend despite the fact you've been a good dog for 50 years because the Prince has decided there's too many Kindred in the city.&quot;<br /> * An Elder Blood Bonds or Dominates you and keeps you as their mind-warped slave for a decade, torturing you like the Purple Man did Jessica Jones.<br /> <br /> BLOODLINES does a decent job of making it clear how confusing and awful the Camarilla system can be if you're not one of the In-Crowd. You get Embraced, your sire murdered, almost executed yourself, and then thrown out on the street to survive by hook or by crook. If you're not already rich and don't have Social Powers, you may be living in abandoned homes and drinking from rats or hobos.<br /> <br /> Being a vampire can SUCK and you may wonder why you support the gerontocracy. Answer? You don't. Unless you're part of the gerontocracy, you're either an Anarch or one of the many vampires who smartly keep their head down and hope to stay out of this.<br /> <br /> There are few other options.<br /> <br /> Anarchs can be and largely are every bit the same kind of assholes the Camarilla are--but they talk a good game about freedom, brotherhood, and venting your anger. Also, if the Prince's Sheriff is around, he's less likely to randomly stake and leave you for the Sun if you have your five good buddies around.<br /> <br /> Which is why coteries are more something for Anarchs than Elders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-01-2022, 04:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T20:57:18-07:00","id":1485448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485414#post1485414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Anarch could be someone who believes in representative or direct democracy. It could be someone who believes in some kind of libertarian utopian. It could be an archconservative vampire who prefers who it was in the Dark Ages BEFORE the Anarch Revolt when Princes could do anything without a Justicar or Conclave interfering. It could be someone who believes there should be a single Lord of the Vampires that all other vampires obey (don't laugh, that's essentially the perspective of the Sabbat with Caine as King and since he's absent our Regent will do, and the Sabbat are supposed to be the original Anarchs). And of course, it could just be criminal thugs who want an excuse/cover for their own crimes. And much of the time, an &quot;Anarch&quot; is just someone the local Prince is crapping o</div> </div> </div> </div>True. And one of the reasons Requiem's Carthians book ended up giving me a lot of useful things to think about regarding Anarchs. (In a similar vein, the Invictus book was really useful for the Camarilla.) You can have a group of Anarchs who are essentially 1920s Italian Fascists (or its Marcus Garvey led African American counterpart) alongside a Hippy commune and an outlaw biker gang, and all of them be legit Anarchs. Likewise the clique of coffee house intellectual anarchists, a bunch of vampire nuns, and that Fake Rapper from the original Brujah clanbook. It's part of why I find them fun. (But I also like using a lot of Ventrue, Lasombra, and Setites as Anarchs, so my tastes are wierd.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T21:02:52-07:00","id":1485449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485448#post1485448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. And one of the reasons Requiem's Carthians book ended up giving me a lot of useful things to think about regarding Anarchs. (In a similar vein, the Invictus book was really useful for the Camarilla.) You can have a group of Anarchs who are essentially 1920s Italian Fascists (or its Marcus Garvey led African American counterpart) alongside a Hippy commune and an outlaw biker gang, and all of them be legit Anarchs. Likewise the clique of coffee house intellectual anarchists, a bunch of vampire nuns, and that Fake Rapper from the original Brujah clanbook. It's part of why I find them fun. (But I also like using a lot of Ventrue, Lasombra, and Setites as Anarchs, so my tastes are wierd.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I like weird. Weird can be good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 07-01-2022, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T01:12:23-07:00","id":1485460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485448#post1485448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True. And one of the reasons Requiem's Carthians book ended up giving me a lot of useful things to think about regarding Anarchs. (In a similar vein, the Invictus book was really useful for the Camarilla.) You can have a group of Anarchs who are essentially 1920s Italian Fascists (or its Marcus Garvey led African American counterpart) alongside a Hippy commune and an outlaw biker gang, and all of them be legit Anarchs. Likewise the clique of coffee house intellectual anarchists, a bunch of vampire nuns, and that Fake Rapper from the original Brujah clanbook. It's part of why I find them fun. (But I also like using a lot of Ventrue, Lasombra, and Setites as Anarchs, so my tastes are wierd.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I feel like it's weird they didn't take MORE from Requiem regarding the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> I've felt a lot of Requiem got co-opted for V5 and this isn't an insult. It's like how a huge amount of ULTIMATE Marvel ended up in the mainstream comicsverse and MCU.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of good ideas.<br /> <br /> Part of what makes the Carthians so interesting is that there's a massive IQ boost to the Anarchs in that the majority of them are less likey to be leather-jacket wearing thugs and more likely to be University educated thinkers who question the validity of a Feudal system in Modern times.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T01:51:27-07:00","id":1485463,"title":"","content":"I keep thinking it would be interesting to go back and try to redesign LA by Night circa 1992 with the benefits of hindsight, better access to research and information on various things, and a much more developed take on the Anarchs and how the &quot;Free States&quot; would function. Also a better eye to history. (I would really prefer the Anarch takeover of LA to happen in the late 60s or so, mainly because I think if you are doing Classic Film Noir Vampire in 40s and 50s LA, it works better as a Camarilla city, at least IMO.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T03:56:48-07:00","id":1485478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485463#post1485463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep thinking it would be interesting to go back and try to redesign LA by Night circa 1992 with the benefits of hindsight, better access to research and information on various things, and a much more developed take on the Anarchs and how the &quot;Free States&quot; would function. Also a better eye to history. (I would really prefer the Anarch takeover of LA to happen in the late 60s or so, mainly because I think if you are doing Classic Film Noir Vampire in 40s and 50s LA, it works better as a Camarilla city, at least IMO.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Which kind of gets into the issue of the fact the books have never really done a great job of establishing what an Anarch domain looks like. The Los Angeles domains are basically &quot;shittier Princedoms&quot; and there's no Maldavis or even Anita Wainwright alternatives. It's probably the saddest thing you can say about LA by Night that Louis Fortier seems like the best buy to be under and he's the most blatantly Camarilla-esque.<br /> <br /> LA By Night the web series shows a much better run Anarch domain under Isaac Abrams and that IS basically &quot;A Prince by any other name&quot; too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T06:34:23-07:00","id":1485494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485437#post1485437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Why be an Anarch? I mean, the reason is obvious: feudalism sucks if you're not the king.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>In many, many fuedal societies, the king was just another noble with a better title and more burdens. Being a duke is great, being an earl is great, being a count is great, being a barron is pretty good, being a knight has great perks: Even the lowliest vampire (13th gen or better) gets to have his own fief and abuse his powers to live a life of luxury. Why start a revolution when you're already in the elite club? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a lot of fans are not taking the time to recognize how fundamentally INSANE the situation is. </div> </div> </div>It isn't, it's a pretty good mirror of the real world. The real world is insane, Vampires are nothing special. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're used to &quot;buying in&quot; to the oddities of a RPG so they ignore that almost everyone not born into the Ventrue, Toreador, or Tremere will be inclined to Anarchism. </div> </div> </div>1: It's interesting that you list the &quot;rich and priveledged clans&quot; as the ones who don't go anarch when the reality is that the Toreador are probably second only to brujah when it comes to the most anarchs. What makes a vampire rebel or not isn't how rich, white and &quot;priveledged&quot; their sire is, but the selectiveness of the sire when choosing childer and the family dynamic concerning their sire and their clanmates. This is why tightly knit groups like the Ventrue, Tremere and <b>Nosferatu</b> have very few Anarchs while the clans prone to infighting or overly lax parenting like the Toreador, Brujah or Gangrel are swarming with anarchs. <br /> <br /> 2- We're not playing ourselves, we're putting ourselves in the shoes of characters that are likely to be sired. IE someone suited for undead life IE not a soft hearted liberal that wants to work against the systemic injustice that actually benefits their new state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T07:24:18-07:00","id":1485505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485494#post1485494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In many, many fuedal societies, the king was just another noble with a better title and more burdens. Being a duke is great, being an earl is great, being a count is great, being a barron is pretty good, being a knight has great perks: Even the lowliest vampire (13th gen or better) gets to have his own fief and abuse his powers to live a life of luxury. Why start a revolution when you're already in the elite club?</div> </div> </div> </div>And then you have the thinbloods and other illegal embraces who are basically Anarch simply by existing. If the status quo says you have to die for the greater good it\u2019s not surprising those individuals might band together to attempt an overthrow of the establishment.<br /> <br /> The Book of Nod had verses about taking in the orphan for probably that exact reason\u2026 which of course get ignored and create a self-fulfilling prophecy. Back people into a corner and they\u2019ll do things they never thought themselves capable of to survive.<br /> <br /> Something like that is far more likely to be the nucleus of a genuine Anarch realm\u2026 a place where the Prince was weak or sloppy enough that a band of those condemned to death by Camarilla standards was able to take them out and now has to figure out some way to keep the Camarilla from coming back and killing them all.<br /> <br /> Ironically, instead of an undead free-for-all, I could see such a territory actually looking at the surface level like a place with an especially heavy Hunter presence, as the members don\u2019t make their locations and positions within the new social structure obvious when an Archon rolls into town and Camarilla vampires tend to go missing if they seem to be making moves towards staying in the area.<br /> <br /> With access to fewer high end disciplines and many thinbloods unable to ghoul many of the telltale signs of vampric control over the local government would also tend to less pronounced or absent altogether. If presenting the territory to a traditional PC coiterie (i.e. 13th Gen and lower non-Anarchs) you could really play with the creepy dearth of Kindred activity coupled with the feeling of being watched.<br /> <br /> Such an Anarch territory is probably organized more like cells of an insurgency (or Hunters) than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T08:24:52-07:00","id":1485507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485505#post1485505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then you have the thinbloods and other illegal embraces who are basically Anarch simply by existing. If the status quo says you have to die for the greater good it\u2019s not surprising those individuals might band together to attempt an overthrow of the establishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinbloods and illegal embraces are both rare and weak, while also lacking the information needed necessary to organize. The idea that they'd be a serious threat is very funny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T10:37:40-07:00","id":1485522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485478#post1485478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which kind of gets into the issue of the fact the books have never really done a great job of establishing what an Anarch domain looks like. The Los Angeles domains are basically &amp;quot;shittier Princedoms&amp;quot; and there's no Maldavis or even Anita Wainwright alternatives.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my 1991 game Anita Wainwright has just arrived to LA after having to leave Chicago. She has made changing the baronies mess into a better society.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, in a more serious note, I agree that the Anarchs are not anarchists. But still, looking at the politics of anarchism we can better think on how a complex society without a single central power can function without being in s perpetual state of war","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T11:54:52-07:00","id":1485524,"title":"","content":"Dull and mediocre might be worse than actually bad. Actually bad is memorable. But we forget the mediocre. And the LA by Night book was mediocre. And unfortunately this made Anarchs dull, if only by association. <br /> <br /> The live-play series was more interesting and a new book on the city, at least partly based on the series would have potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T12:01:20-07:00","id":1485525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485478#post1485478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which kind of gets into the issue of the fact the books have never really done a great job of establishing what an Anarch domain looks like. The Los Angeles domains are basically &quot;shittier Princedoms&quot; and there's no Maldavis or even Anita Wainwright alternatives. It's probably the saddest thing you can say about LA by Night that Louis Fortier seems like the best buy to be under and he's the most blatantly Camarilla-esque.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. In hindsight, I think one of the biggest missed opportunities with the 2nd ed By Night books is that they didn't try to make each one a different example of how vampire politics could work. If 1st ed Chicago is the baseline example of a powerful tyrant prince with a strong primogen that could challenge him if they felt like it and various potential Camarilla, Anarch, and even Sabbat challengers around the edges (and 2nd ed is what happens when said prince is removed), the rest should try to be something different. LA should show how an Anarch run city <i>can</i> function (even if more than a few of the leaders are total hypocrites or slightly naive idealists); Berlin should show how that city's recent history has resulted in a unique vampire political situation of two rival but equally legitimate courts (perhaps one at least making the pretense of being Anarch/Independent friendly to bolster its standing); DC should probably have been a city ruled by its Primogen and only a figurehead prince (or none at all); Montreal how a Sabbat city based primarily around its elder &quot;clergy&quot; looks while a place like Detroit is how one run entirely at the pack level functions, and Mexico City is a mid-point/mix of the two. Maybe New Orleans should have been the city were most of the Camarilla positions of power were held by Brujah, Nosferatu, Gangrel, and Malkavians. Hong Kong as a place Western and Eastern kindred (whatever form the latter take) are able to at least pretend to function properly together. And so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T12:03:48-07:00","id":1485526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485507#post1485507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Thinbloods and illegal embraces are both rare and weak, </b>while also lacking the information needed necessary to organize. The idea that they'd be a serious threat is very funny.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/ishethough.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Are they, though?<br /> <br /> I mean, there's about 100K vampires in the world at any given time and the number of Thin Bloods and Caitiff we have in sample characters aren't any less (if not slightly more) than we have of other Clans. Plus, the fact the Camarilla thought Caitiff, illegal Embraces, and Thin Bloods were numerous that they created an entire new position solely for the purposes of eliminating them. Scourges wouldn't exist if there weren't a SHIT TON of illegal Embraces and Thin Bloods.<br /> <br /> Hell, Thin Bloods are so common they have their own book in Revised, they have their own Clan Entry in V5, and they apparently are numerous enough to have numerous factions like Cleavers, Alchemists, and so on.<br /> <br /> V5 seems to be going with the idea that High Generation and Thin Blood vampires are the majority these days. Which is why it's the Time of Thin Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-01-2022, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T12:04:23-07:00","id":1485527,"title":"","content":"This topic prompted me to review some of my old notes on the Free States and my old, second hand copy of LAbN. I wanted to see what I had written in terms of Anarch factions and Baronies that would be in my chronicle's version of the Free States. So I reread the description of Jeremy MacNeil in LAbN and something popped out that I had not considered before.<br /> <br /> We're told that Jeremy was born in 1631 and his clan fought on behalf of Charles I. He was embraced in 1657. This means as a young mortal that Jeremy would have fought in the English Civil Wars. His enemy would not have been the king (who upheld the idea of the divine rights of kings and probably the idea of absolute monarchy). His enemy would have been Parliament. This is not what we would normally expect from someone who became an &quot;Anarch&quot;. The most likely image of a tyrant then, in Jeremy MacNeil's eyes, would be Oliver Cromwell. I find this very interesting.<br /> <br /> It's also important to note that in VtM's lore, the Wars of the Three Kingdoms was a prolonged power struggle by the Toreador (as Scotland was a Toreador bastion, and they held influence in the Stuart Dynasty that came from Scotland) against the Ventrue (who had influence in Parliament). This should have influenced his perception of Vampire politics.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, his biography notes he later went to Ireland to fight there. There's actually not many prominent Irish rebellions after 1657 and when he departed for America (as he was there during the War of Independence). The most likely one was the Jacobite War in Ireland after the Glorious Revolution. This may simply be because at this point in time he hates the English (or perhaps as a Brujah, sees the Ventrue in England as the enemy), but I find it noteworthy that once again Jeremy is on the &quot;wrong side&quot; of what we would expect an Anarch to be. (An interesting idea is that around this the British Toreador might have seen Jeremy as a useful ally or pawn in their struggles against the Ventrue.) It's not until he arrives in the British colonies in America that the mortal side of things begin to conform to what we would expect of an Anarch.<br /> <br /> I bring this up because it is not something that is apparent. I doubt the original writers of Jeremy MacNeil intended it. But I think it's something to be considered when we think about the character of Jeremy MacNeil.<br /> <br /> Now I would not expect an uneducated Highlands warrior with a Rebel Nature to have any real political beliefs or ideology. Most of his views of freedom likely came later while he was a vampire. And probably more because of his Rebel nature than a coherent philosophical view. He seems to be principled and have an instinctive grasp on injustice, but he's probably not very politically astute or motivated. But as a natural leader of men, he attracts a lot of others who feel the same way on local issues.<br /> <br /> It makes sense then that while he is a symbol of the modern Anarchs, that it is others who are producing anything like a political manifesto. Salvador Garcia wrote the Status Perfectus and the Anarch Manifesto. However, Jeremy is smart. He's probably self-educated himself during his existence as a vampire, and like many autodidacts he has an eclectic view on things. It shouldn't be a surprise that his primary friend and ally, Crispus Attucks, is described as &quot;not a deep thinker.&quot;<br /> <br /> I wonder if a good model for Jeremy MacNeil might possibly be Ernst Junger, another man who was a non-conformist, a warrior, originally loyal to a monarchy, once considered to be a &quot;conservative revolutionary&quot; but who increasingly rejected government's attempts to control people. Eventually Junger would develop the concept of an &quot;Anarch&quot; - as opposed to an anarchist. An Anarch championed the <i>solitary individual who remains true to himself</i> regardless of whatever external circumstances happened to be present. Junger would develop his theory on the Anarch more as philosophical problem for the individual than a political one for society. Eventually he describes that the Anarch is to anarchy what a monarch is to monarchy. The Anarch only wants to rule himself, and instead of opposing forms of government like an anarchist, just ignores them and acts appropriately. The Anarch represents total freedom and mankind's truest form, a kind of natural ubermensch that people should aspire to.<br /> <br /> While I don't think Ernst Junger's work served as inspiration to the creation of the character of Jeremy MacNeil, I feel it is in many ways appropriate to it. We don't need to adopt Junger's philosophy, just take certain elements and apply them to MacNeil. It would explain his reluctance to govern or develop any kind of political manifesto. He just wants to be left alone, and feels other vampires should feel that way too. He just doesn't have any political solution to the problem that others want power, that justice is needed to be imposed on the criminal element, or that there is a competition for scarce resources. Instead, he just falls back on &quot;be a man and enforce justice yourself if someone tries to violate you.&quot; At least I feel that more properly depicts MacNeil than the idea that he is some kind of Social Darwinist who sees the strong winnowing out the weak. It would be more like an idea of &quot;If you want to be free, only YOU can do that. I can't make you free yourself.&quot;<br /> <br /> There was an old notion that Anarchs believed in a &quot;Libertas&quot;, which like Humanity, was something &quot;real&quot; for a vampire and meant vampires should be free. It was a strange concept, and it doesn't seem to have been promoted much in the books after the Anarch Cookbook (I don't know if this got much attention in V20 or V5). But if we take the idea seriously, we could even see Jeremy's attitude as being &quot;Hey, dummy, you need to increase your Libertas and fight back or you'll never truly be free.&quot; Well, at least it'd be an excuse.<br /> <br /> That's why he and his coterie of friends defend their territory of Los Angeles, but he mostly refuses to play any additional role in &quot;the Movement.&quot; He doesn't want one because he doesn't want power over others although he believes the Camarilla needs to end for Kindred freedom to happen, and he is willing to fight. He may be politically naive, but very principled as an individual. He's just doomed to be a symbol - a &quot;modern day Patricia of Bolingbroke&quot;, and only get involved in local matters occasionally when he sees the local situation deteriorating too much and affecting him. In so far that he plays a useful role for the Anarch Movement, it would to provide a safe haven for other Anarchs who are incapable of ruling a domain (a barony) of their own, and need a local protector. Some of these theorists and provocateurs can then develop their politics and actions, and they perpetuate the idea that their &quot;patron&quot; and protector MacNeil is an important force for the Anarchs. If we want a positive view of MacNeil's barony, it would be as an &quot;incubator&quot; of ideas for the Anarch movement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T12:18:16-07:00","id":1485528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485494#post1485494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In many, many fuedal societies, the king was just another noble with a better title and more burdens. Being a duke is great, being an earl is great, being a count is great, being a barron is pretty good, being a knight has great perks: Even the lowliest vampire (13th gen or better) gets to have his own fief and abuse his powers to live a life of luxury. Why start a revolution when you're already in the elite club?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and the word for the aristocracy in vampire society is the Harpies and the Primogen. Mind you, I don't think we're going to agree on this because you've always gone with the idea that every vampire is a noble while I've always gone with the idea that the majority of vampires are peasants. I've always felt the Camarilla would love to reduce the vampire populatioin by about 90% and avoid having to deal with all of these children among themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It isn't, it's a pretty good mirror of the real world. The real world is insane, Vampires are nothing special. </div> </div> </div>I agree, which is why conflict exists in our world as well. But to reframe the issue, vampire society is fundamentally a violent power-based system. The Anarchs exist because there's no reward for loyalty or hard work. The best way to advance in the Camarilla is to find someone weak and murder them to take their stuff. The powerful never die out and pass down their power so the only way to move up in the world is to make an opening.<br /> <br /> So you either reject the system entirely (Anarchs) or try to make allies to destroy your enemies. Which does fit in with those people who believe Anarchs tend to be a temporary state. Eventually, you either die or sell out as Harvey Dent said differently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1: It's interesting that you list the &quot;rich and priveledged clans&quot; as the ones who don't go anarch when the reality is that the Toreador are probably second only to brujah when it comes to the most anarchs. What makes a vampire rebel or not isn't how rich, white and &quot;priveledged&quot; their sire is, but the selectiveness of the sire when choosing childer and the family dynamic concerning their sire and their clanmates. This is why tightly knit groups like the Ventrue, Tremere and <b>Nosferatu</b> have very few Anarchs while the clans prone to infighting or overly lax parenting like the Toreador, Brujah or Gangrel are swarming with anarchs.<br /> <br /> 2- We're not playing ourselves, we're putting ourselves in the shoes of characters that are likely to be sired. IE someone suited for undead life IE not a soft hearted liberal that wants to work against the systemic injustice that actually benefits their new state. </div> </div> </div>1. I tend to view the membership in the Anarchs as being primarily Brujah and Caitiff but my view is the Catiff are probably the largest of the Clans. This is another case where there's no hard figures but I've viewed a condition of the Modern Nights as the Catiff and Thin Bloods as having exploded in population. Enough to the point that they're their own power base and Clan really even without Joseph Panders. After that, Gangrel but the thing is the Gangrel didn't have as much Anarch-sympathy as the Brujah because they just leave whenever they get too much into a Prince's bad graces. They have freedom because they live on the edges of society so there's less pressure to fight the man.<br /> <br /> 2. I think that's an interesting case to examine about Embracing. One post from the old WW forum was like, &quot;I don't get why so many Embraces are so seemingly random.&quot; He wrote a long essay I still remember where he said that he presumed Vampires would carefully vet their childer and choose the absolute best of the best in terms of psychology as well as skill set plus also a variety of other factors.<br /> <br /> The responses to him was that a lot of gamers felt that, in fact, vampires would embrace people for much-much more arbitrary reasons.<br /> <br /> * Guilt based emergency transformation (Oops, I frenzied and ate a ten year old)<br /> <br /> * Embracing your friends and loved ones because you don't want them to die or need companionship. (Also, Embracing a woman or man because you want to bang them/drink from them which I assume is as common as sexual need in RL)<br /> <br /> * Embracing for a specific need (Lodin embraced Capone to control organized crime, Lestat originally was written to have Embraced Louis because he was broke and Louis was a plantation owner)<br /> <br /> * Embracing them as cannon fodder or as a specific weapon. Which the Anarchs might not do as much as the Sabbat but certainly probably do a reasonable amount.<br /> <br /> * Revenge Embracing which seems more common than people thinks with the Nosferatu, Blood Bond, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T12:20:45-07:00","id":1485529,"title":"","content":"As a historian I'd probably comment feudalism isn't 'insane'. It's a pretty solid system for its period, stable laws for the transfer of power and a well defined layout for the state works. Then again the carmarilla is late feudal anyway.<br /> <br /> Conversly the anarchs are actually step bellow the feudal system as psuado tribal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T12:22:56-07:00","id":1485531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485527#post1485527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes sense then that while he is a symbol of the modern Anarchs, that it is others who are producing anything like a political manifesto. Salvador Garcia wrote the Status Perfectus and the Anarch Manifesto. However, Jeremy is smart. He's probably self-educated himself during his existence as a vampire, and like many autodidacts he has an eclectic view on things. It shouldn't be a surprise that his primary friend and ally, Crispus Attucks, is described as &quot;not a deep thinker.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent write-up.<br /> <br /> Another thing to note, though, that I think should be brought up is Salvador Garcia is an interesting contrast himself. The father of the Anarch Movement is a communist revolutionary who was heavily involved in massive war crimes during the Spanish Civil War and later would be actively working among the communist revolutionaries fostered by the authoritarian Soviet Union (Brujah Council?). He's someone who absolutely sees no contradiction in fighting for &quot;freedom&quot; on behalf of a bunch of individuals who are completely against any form of democracy or leadership from the people as long as they're fighting &quot;for&quot; the people.<br /> <br /> I easily imagine him as the kind of self-centered Anarch hypocrite who kills anyone who dissents against the leadership as class traitors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485529#post1485529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a historian I'd probably comment feudalism isn't 'insane'. It's a pretty solid system for its period, stable laws for the transfer of power and a well defined layout for the state works. Then again the carmarilla is late feudal anyway.<br /> <br /> Conversly the anarchs are actually step bellow the feudal system as psuado tribal</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether you agree or not, I find the idea that a person who was raised in a time of the 20th and 21st century to react to the idea of absolute monarchy as well as capital punishment by unelected aristocracy to be something they would find abnormal as well as abhorrent.<br /> <br /> Unless your character works for the mafia, it's hard to believe they have any reason to think it is a system to be loyal to.<br /> <br /> As for the Anarchs being tribal, I feel that's a somewhat antiquated view of things as plenty of tribal cultures have personal codes of ethics and laws that are far fairer than Medievalism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-01-2022, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T13:34:42-07:00","id":1485541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485326#post1485326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now let's look at an Anarch &amp;quot;domain&amp;quot;. There's a bunch of gangs. They squabble openly for territory, only joining forces when there's an invasion by the Sabbat or Camarilla. There's nothing much to do in an Anarch domain except prepare your haven for the next territorial gang squabble or Sabbat/Cammy invasion.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've just described Necromunda setting. And trust me there are many things to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T16:33:50-07:00","id":1485567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485531#post1485531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whether you agree or not, I find the idea that a person who was raised in a time of the 20th and 21st century to react to the idea of absolute monarchy as well as capital punishment by unelected aristocracy to be something they would find abnormal as well as abhorrent.<br /> <br /> Unless your character works for the mafia, it's hard to believe they have any reason to think it is a system to be loyal to.<br /> <br /> As for the Anarchs being tribal, I feel that's a somewhat antiquated view of things as plenty of tribal cultures have personal codes of ethics and laws that are far fairer than Medievalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>A number of things<br /> -a feudal society is not the same as an absolute monarchy.<br /> -the carmarilla genrally isn't an absolute an absolute monarchy anyway even locally. More of decentralised obligarchy if anything.<br /> -a substantial number of people in 20th and 21st century peoples and cultures are ruled by autocratic obligarchies who can and will kill you. To a worrying degree in fact.<br /> -vampiric society cannot replicate human economics, their ecology is just too alien.<br /> <br /> As for tribal societies being nicer and more humane than feudal societies....not really no. I've never heard that put forward outside of hyper romanticised thinking. You could probably argue they're &quot;as bad&quot; but most pre modern societies have a problem with endemic violence and kratocratic tendencies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-01-2022, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T16:47:38-07:00","id":1485568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485567#post1485567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A number of things<br /> -a feudal society is not the same as an absolute monarchy.<br /> -the carmarilla genrally isn't an absolute an absolute monarchy anyway even locally. More of decentralised obligarchy if anything.<br /> -a substantial number of people in 20th and 21st century peoples and cultures are ruled by autocratic obligarchies who can and will kill you. To a worrying degree in fact.<br /> -vampiric society cannot replicate human society, their ecology is just too alien.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as if none of this would remotely effect the culture shock, horror, and disgust that a person Embraced would feel upon being introduced to Kindred society. You may disagree but I think the point still holds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for tribal societies being nicer and more humane than feudal societies....not really no. I've never heard that put forward outside of hyper romanticised thinking. You could probably argue they're &quot;as bad&quot; but most pre modern societies have a problem with endemic violence and kratocratic tendencies. </div> </div> </div>Basically, I tend to have the view that tribal societies are primarily viewed through the &quot;primitivism&quot; lens of historians who are engaged in a great deal of cultural posturing. The dismissal of their own societies and traditions for supposed Western advancement. Basically, &quot;tribal&quot; gets applied to a lot of complex cultures even today.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T16:49:26-07:00","id":1485569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485494#post1485494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In many, many fuedal societies, the king was just another noble with a better title and more burdens. Being a duke is great, being an earl is great, being a count is great, being a barron is pretty good, being a knight has great perks: Even the lowliest vampire (13th gen or better) gets to have his own fief and abuse his powers to live a life of luxury. Why start a revolution when you're already in the elite club?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stuff like this is all well and good until you remember that if Barons, Counts, and Dukes were satisfied with how well off they were, no King would ever have had to fear for their crown. For better or worse, few people in power are ever satisfied with their power. <br /> <br /> More often or not, they'd rather be &quot;first in a village, rather than second in Rome.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T17:19:07-07:00","id":1485573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485568#post1485568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel as if none of this would remotely effect the culture shock, horror, and disgust that a person Embraced would feel upon being introduced to Kindred society. You may disagree but I think the point still holds.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Basically, I tend to have the view that tribal societies are primarily viewed through the &quot;primitivism&quot; lens of historians who are engaged in a great deal of cultural posturing. The dismissal of their own societies and traditions for supposed Western advancement. Basically, &quot;tribal&quot; gets applied to a lot of complex cultures even today.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly but unless you've been raised explicitly in a mid 21st century Liberal democracy (and not involved in organized crime.) I don't think it would... I personally think from historical and cultural trends that once you get your turf you probably don't care. Which is frankly, quite frightening in its own way.<br /> <br /> ......and by contrast you get people who romanticise the various cultures to a absurd degree. Tribal cultures are not 'nicer' than feudal ones, the golden horde wernt on a humanitarian mission when they crushed the turks and feudal poles.<br /> <br /> Its also probably worth noting that feudal cultures typically evolve from tribal and a lot of the cultures obliterated or decimated in the early modern period wernt tribal. Mughal India, the aztec empire and imperial China for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-01-2022, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T17:20:08-07:00","id":1485574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485569#post1485569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stuff like this is all well and good until you remember that if Barons, Counts, and Dukes were satisfied with how well off they were, no King would ever have had to fear for their crown. For better or worse, few people in power are ever satisfied with their power.<br /> <br /> More often or not, they'd rather be &quot;first in a village, rather than second in Rome.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I also am going to state the &quot;13th generation vampires living lives of luxury&quot; thing is a pretty weird take as we have vampires living in the sewers, abandoned buildings, and struggling from night to night to get food without killing anyone (or even with killing someone).<br /> <br /> You can very easily turn a city that is 100% Camarilla and happy to one that isn't just by saying, &quot;All of the City's territory is taken. You either have to drive out to the boonies to feed, move on, or feed in a designated area like the Rack.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is I think <b>something the ST should determine ahead of time</b> before any game because it could vary from city to city.<br /> <br /> 1. How much territory is &quot;free&quot; for new vampires?<br /> <br /> 2. How does the Camarilla deal with poachers?<br /> <br /> 3. How many vampires exist outside the Camarilla's power structure? Anarchs, Independents, or rogues?<br /> <br /> 4. How ruthless is the Prince? (I generally use a 3 strike law: 1. Warning or a beating. 2. Torture. 3. Final Death<br /> <br /> 5. What is the quality of life for a Neonate?<br /> <br /> It really depends I suppose on how antagonistic you want your city to be and that's a good thing for a game. Because obviously you WANT conflict. Otherwise there's no game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T17:22:30-07:00","id":1485575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485573#post1485573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its also probably worth noting that feudal cultures typically evolve from tribal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, I was thinking of the Iroquois Confederacy and the general dismissal its culture got from Europeans. Also, the fact that many modern tribal societies exist while feudalism is a (thankfully) mostly dead system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T19:25:30-07:00","id":1485583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485531#post1485531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Excellent write-up.<br /> <br /> Another thing to note, though, that I think should be brought up is Salvador Garcia is an interesting contrast himself. The father of the Anarch Movement is a communist revolutionary who was heavily involved in massive war crimes during the Spanish Civil War and later would be actively working among the communist revolutionaries fostered by the authoritarian Soviet Union (Brujah Council?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Salvador Garc\u00eda is not a communist revolutionary, he is an anarcho communist. In his LAbN is clearly explicited that he was an Andalusian peasant and he belonged to the Mano Negra (which is still debated by historians whether it actually existed or was anti anarchist propaganda). He's mentioned to have fighted in Barcelona during the civil war; at thiat time anarchisrs were much more numerous than communists in the Republican army, so much that at some point, the government betrayed and attacked them in return from Stalin's help (tanks and planes)<br /> On a side note, I find your comments about massive war crimes distateful to say the least. The Spanish anarchists were fighting against an illegal fascist coup, actually supported by the Italian and German governments. Probably there were excesses on their side too, but calling them massive war crimes is beyond the pale. If you are going to go that route, you should apply the same criteria to what the USA government did in Dresde or Hiroshima and say that all American soldiers during WW2 participated in massive war crimes and collaborated with totalitarian Stalinism","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T19:59:42-07:00","id":1485584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485583#post1485583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Salvador Garc\u00eda is not a communist revolutionary, he is an anarcho communist. In his LAbN is clearly explicited that he was an Andalusian peasant and he belonged to the Mano Negra (which is still debated by historians whether it actually existed or was anti anarchist propaganda). He's mentioned to have fighted in Barcelona during the civil war; at thiat time anarchisrs were much more numerous than communists in the Republican army, so much that at some point, the government betrayed and attacked them in return from Stalin's help (tanks and planes)<br /> <br /> On a side note, I find your comments about massive war crimes distateful to say the least. The Spanish anarchists were fighting against an illegal fascist coup, actually supported by the Italian and German governments. Probably there were excesses on their side too, but calling them massive war crimes is beyond the pale. If you are going to go that route, you should apply the same criteria to what the USA government did in Dresde or Hiroshima and say that all American soldiers during WW2 participated in massive war crimes and collaborated with totalitarian Stalinism</div> </div> </div> </div>Avoiding RL politics (I am an anarchist in RL) and military history, my interpretation of Salvador was definitely Marxist communist over anarcho-communist.<br /> <br /> I stand corrected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-01-2022, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T20:53:52-07:00","id":1485592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485584#post1485584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Avoiding RL politics (I am an anarchist in RL) and military history, my interpretation of Salvador was definitely Marxist communist over anarcho-communist.<br /> <br /> I stand corrected.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I apologize if I came out too strong on you, I misread your comments as classical anti left, anti anarchist attacks, and not as a nuanced take on the Spanish Civil War. I am also an anarcho pacifist and you will find me arguing against anarcho communists against the role of revolutionary violence. <br /> My point stands on Salvador Garc\u00eda stands. As am Andalucian 19th century anarchist he is probably extremely anti authoritarian and anti communist. I envision him supporting the Latin American guerrillas against both USA backed governments AND Soviet influence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T21:17:16-07:00","id":1485596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485574#post1485574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also am going to state the &quot;13th generation vampires living lives of luxury&quot; thing is a pretty weird take as we have vampires living in the sewers, abandoned buildings, and struggling from night to night to get food without killing anyone (or even with killing someone).<br /> <br /> You can very easily turn a city that is 100% Camarilla and happy to one that isn't just by saying, &quot;All of the City's territory is taken. You either have to drive out to the boonies to feed, move on, or feed in a designated area like the Rack.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is I think <b>something the ST should determine ahead of time</b> before any game because it could vary from city to city.<br /> <br /> 1. How much territory is &quot;free&quot; for new vampires?<br /> <br /> 2. How does the Camarilla deal with poachers?<br /> <br /> 3. How many vampires exist outside the Camarilla's power structure? Anarchs, Independents, or rogues?<br /> <br /> 4. How ruthless is the Prince? (I generally use a 3 strike law: 1. Warning or a beating. 2. Torture. 3. Final Death<br /> <br /> 5. What is the quality of life for a Neonate?<br /> <br /> It really depends I suppose on how antagonistic you want your city to be and that's a good thing for a game. Because obviously you WANT conflict. Otherwise there's no game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunting territory really should come up more than it does. In practice, most ST's are trying to tell a story about fancy parties, detective work, and ass-kicking. I think those sort of hunting territory limitations rarely come up because it gets in the way of the three main things most ST's are trying to tell a story about. Consequently, hunting is done in a way that is usually perfunctory. The PC rolls his Predator pool, if they succeed, there is a very short, simple scene of them punching that hobo in an alley, seducing that guy in a club, whathaveyou.<br /> <br /> They mark down their hunger, and back we go to the fancy-parties/detective-work/ass-kicking that is 99% of the ST's story.<br /> <br /> If they fail, there is some consequences like covering up that murder, running from a hunter, whathaveyou. Dealing with failure tends to take a bit longer, but it is still usually dealt with in a quick way, because it is ultimately just a speedbump in the ST's story of fancy-parties, detective work, and ass-kicking.<br /> <br /> A story in which the players find that they simply can not hunt, because everywhere they could hope to hunt is someone's domain, is almost unheard of in my experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T21:29:38-07:00","id":1485597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485596#post1485596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A story in which the players find that they simply can not hunt, because everywhere they could hope to hunt is someone's domain, is almost unheard of in my experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunting as a general rule is something that I think most people don't do very often as it gets in the way of the &quot;fun&quot; parts of the game. However, I've used it a few times in my game as a source of adventure hooks.<br /> <br /> * The PCs have their own territory and there's a vampire who has killed some humans that they were fond of or just draws attention to them.<br /> * The PCs have a friend of theirs who an Elder is royally at pissed at. They drank from one fo their vessels and the mortal is either comatose or dying because they didn't realize they'd already been fed from.<br /> * The Pcs find their own herd's home area has been awarded to another vampire by the Prince. This may be a deliberate slight or even horrific insult (one of the PCs found that the Prince gave their SISTER to a vampire as a Blood Doll).<br /> * The PCs find that Anarchs regularly get beaten up for wandering into the wrong territory like a Southern Sheriff to &quot;undesirables.&quot; I encourage people looking to Rambo: First Blood for how a Sheriff might treat them entering an Elder's territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T21:51:05-07:00","id":1485598,"title":"","content":"I think I may use something like this as part of my Cathari Demagogue subplot. Perhaps Cathari packs have claimed all the new territory acquired during the siege of New Orleans and the player pack, being Feral Hearters, are finding it almost ironically impossible to hunt. That would really get under their skin because their hunting of Cammy touchstones was such a vital part of the siege.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T22:21:03-07:00","id":1485600,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485526#post1485526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><img src=\"https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/ishethough.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Are they, though?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">YES</span></span></span><br /> Have you never left the farm? Do you honestly think that a thinblood, in a city, would find other thinbloods before other fullblooded vampires make objections to the fledgling barging in on their territory? Even small Cities are BIG and fledglings without proper education aren't likely to live a week.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Hell, Thin Bloods are so common they have their own book in Revised, they have their own Clan Entry in V5, and they apparently are numerous enough to have numerous factions like Cleavers, Alchemists, and so on.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">V5 seems to be going with the idea that High Generation and Thin Blood vampires are the majority these days. Which is why it's the Time of Thin Blood.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yes but V5 seems to be going with the ideas like &quot; the Cam should become snooty and give up half it's territory to anarchs&quot; and &quot;all the elders should dissapear&quot; so I'd hardly put stock in what V5 does to the setting. </span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">think that's an interesting case to examine about Embracing. One post from the old WW forum was like, &quot;I don't get why so many Embraces are so seemingly random.&quot; He wrote a long essay I still remember where he said that he presumed Vampires would carefully vet their childer and choose the absolute best of the best in terms of psychology as well as skill set plus also a variety of other factors.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The responses to him was that a lot of gamers felt that, in fact, vampires would embrace people for much-much more arbitrary reasons.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yeah they feel that way, and if you ask LARPers they'll also tell you that werewolves have dayjobs and the independent vampire sects like the FoS and Assamites should join together to make their own factions. Let's put it another way: Do politicians make selfish, stupid or evil laws sometimes? absolutely. It regularly makes the news, and these politicians will happily justify their toxic nonsense and pretend to believe they're doing the right thing. However, are the majority of laws selfish, stupid or evil? No. You'll also note that selfish, stupid and evil laws tend to get overturned frequently, while boring, functional laws last for hundreds of years. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> Your example is basically &quot;OP: why do I play with so many people making stupid characters&quot; and then &quot;OP, We have JUSTIFICATION to make stupid characters&quot;. and, y'know, if your ST thinks everyone'll have fun playing their silly characters rather than the same sociopaths, more power to them, but don't assume that just because something's popular with players means that it's popular in setting, otherwise most neonates in modern nights will be 8th generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T22:32:55-07:00","id":1485601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485600#post1485600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you never left the farm? Do you honestly think that a thinblood, in a city, would find other thinbloods before other fullblooded vampires make objections to the fledgling barging in on their territory? Even small Cities are BIG and fledglings without proper education aren't likely to live a week.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, yes, obviously they could and probably do all the time. It's very likely a Thin Blood will meet other Thin Bloods either as their sire's creation or their sire themselves. A vampire who doesn't mind Thin Blooded offspring will probably create plenty of them as they're extremely weak and easy to bully/use but have excellent uses. The Thin Bloods also violate the Masquerade all the time and contact each other over the net and other locations. They also are better acclimated to survival than other Neonates because of their lesser Beasts, lesser sunlight weakness, and ability to survive on blood that would be rancid to a normal vampire.<br /> <br /> Why there's an epidemic of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yes but V5 seems to be going with the ideas like &quot; the Cam should become snooty and give up half it's territory to anarchs&quot; and &quot;all the elders should dissapear&quot; so I'd hardly put stock in what V5 does to the setting. </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Hence why I pointed out the massive outbreak of Caitiff and Thin Bloods is the work of previous editions with OUTCASTS and TIME OF THIN BLOOD. It's not like the idea of there being massive numbers of Clanless is anything new to the setting. It was in the first Chicago by Night where the Caitiff had a half-dozen entries.<br /> <br /> Maldavis, Uriah, Dickie, and Gordon Keaton off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah they feel that way, and if you ask LARPers they'll also tell you that werewolves have dayjobs and the independent vampire sects like the FoS and Assamites should join together to make their own factions. Let's put it another way: Do politicians make selfish, stupid or evil laws sometimes? absolutely. It regularly makes the news, and these politicians will happily justify their toxic nonsense and pretend to believe they're doing the right thing. However, are the majority of laws selfish, stupid or evil? No. You'll also note that selfish, stupid and evil laws tend to get overturned frequently, while boring, functional laws last for hundreds of years. </div> </div> </div>I mean I believe the vast majority of laws throughout history have existed for the purposes of preserving the power and privilege of an elite few at the expenditure of the many. I furthermore believe that leveling between the classes only comes through pressure from the working class. I don't think it ever is done voluntarily by the elite without said pressure. Certainly, I note that slavery existed for thousands of years and has always been abjectly evil.<br /> <br /> So, no, I strongly disagree that &quot;pragmatic laws for the good of the many&quot; are the most common form of law and that tyrants will be overthrown. I believe sometimes they last until their natural lifespan exists and among Kindred that can be centuries or millennia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your example is basically &quot;OP: why do I play with so many people making stupid characters&quot; and then &quot;OP, We have JUSTIFICATION to make stupid characters&quot;. and, y'know, if your ST thinks everyone'll have fun playing their silly characters rather than the same sociopaths, more power to them, but don't assume that just because something's popular with players means that it's popular in setting, otherwise most neonates in modern nights will be 8th generation. </div> </div> </div>I mean the context of the game is what you're going for and playing an Elders game or Pro-Camarilla game is certainly fine for anyone. If LARP was the guiding force for Vampire: The Masquerade, no one would be playing Anarchs and the Camarilla would consist entirely of people scheming all day in funny costumes with the Prince democratically elected from whichever Neonate is paying for the soda. I mean, blood.<br /> <br /> I choose to think very much of 1st Edition as the best V:TM and focus primarily on the view of it as Gothic PUNK primarily. The conflict at the game's core being the War of Ages, Elders vs. Anarchs, and the view that it is one of the Haves and Have Nots.<br /> <br /> Or phrased differently, I view it as Cyberpunk but instead of Corpos versus Street Criminals, it's Elders vs. Neonates. Instead of cyberpnetics, it's Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-02-2022, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T23:08:57-07:00","id":1485602,"title":"","content":"I agree that Vampire took a huge amount of influence from cyberpunk stuff, and related products like Shadowrun. It's notable that Shadowrunners don't really have their own territory. They grudgingly serve the elite, and any cathartic rebellion on their part is against individuals who screwed them over, not the system as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T08:21:04-07:00","id":1485625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485602#post1485602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that Vampire took a huge amount of influence from cyberpunk stuff, and related products like Shadowrun. It's notable that Shadowrunners don't really have their own territory. They grudgingly serve the elite, and any cathartic rebellion on their part is against individuals who screwed them over, not the system as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, oddly, the set up for V:TM is that Anarchs aren't really rebels equivalent but closer to how cyberpunk treats crime bosses.<br /> <br /> Basically, the corpos are the really wealthy and powerful assholes.<br /> <br /> While the crime bosses are a level down but have their own networks and areas of influence. Dirtier, less influential, but also closer to where Edgerunners operate from. Also, every bit as mean and nasty, just more open and honest about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T09:32:21-07:00","id":1485630,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Haquim;n1485320]The title, basically: why do you think we never got a decently flashed out anarch domain? In the years we got loads of Camarilla ones, a few Sabbat ones and even one Autarkis one (Cairo). All we got for Anarchs are contested domains (the former Free State basically) and, recently, a shortt write up for Indianapolis (which is more a Setite city than an Anarch one). Why do you think game designers are so reluctant writing a supplement for a full Anarch domain?<br /> <br /> Edit:I guess it might be a lack of imagination on how to best create such a fractious group of neonates and ancialla who have there own ideas of how to create a better vampire society. They don't have a united vision like the other two major sects or the raw power to back it up. Most of them are of the weaker generations and you would be lucky to encounter any 9th or 10th generation members in there circle who have gotten a real taste of power from the Camarilla and the Sabbat have. That is my two bits in regard why there hasn't been much stuff on the Anarchs outside The Guide To The Anarchs that was published years ago and the more recent one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T00:04:02-07:00","id":1486084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485592#post1485592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point stands on Salvador Garc\u00eda stands. As am Andalucian 19th century anarchist he is probably extremely anti authoritarian and anti communist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since this thread has inspired me to look back at LAbN and develop the Free States for my own chronicles, I've come to certain conclusions on Salvador and his &quot;gang&quot;.<br /> <br /> Jesus Ramirez is the de facto &quot;baron&quot; of La Hermandad in Los Angeles. He rules the &quot;barony&quot; in Salvador's absence. Many, but not all, of its members come out of the Spanish anarchist tradition. Jesus is one of the major leaders in the Los Angeles Free States. But Salvador Garcia is the leader of &quot;the Brotherhood&quot; which is a North American wide (possibly worldwide) secret society of anarchists among vampires. Members are required to swear an oath to each other as well as to the principles for which the Brotherhood ostensibly stands. (Because secret societies and oaths are cool, and if Salvador was a member of the Mano Negra we should have elements like that in our own new fictional society).<br /> <br /> Unless you are in Los Angeles and in the barony Jesus Ramirez controls, you aren't an actual member of La Hermandad. It's a local factor only. But any Anarch anywhere might be a member of the Brotherhood, which would be a secret society of vampire anarchists. Of course, the barony of La Hermandad would be a place of refuge and indoctrination/training for any member of the Brotherhood, and Jesus would welcome a lot of members of the Brotherhood for a while before eventually kicking them out to go back outside and spread the revolution.<br /> <br /> Technically, there is no distinction between La Hermandad and the Brotherhood. It's just that La Hermandad is a particular local &quot;chapter&quot; of the Brotherhood, and an example of what members of the Brotherhoods in other cities hope to recreate locally.<br /> <br /> In some domains, there may be actual coteries of the Brotherhood where every vampire is a member of the Brotherhood. In other domains, members would belong to coteries whose other members might be other Anarchs or even members of the Camarilla, their membership of the Brotherhood either a secret known only to them or perhaps known to other coterie members depending on the specifics. But they all hold to anarchist ideals and are personally loyal to Salvador Garcia.<br /> <br /> Now, I don't know what it would actually mean to be an anarchist vampire as opposed to what a human anarchist believes. A lot of human anarchism relates to economic issues like the means of production which is totally irrelevant to vampires in regards to other vampires. Maybe some kind of self-governing commune in place of the Prince and Primogen, and no individual domains/hunting grounds with every territory being open to all vampires?<br /> <br /> I think having an actual secret society of anarchist vampires among the Anarchs provides some much needed flavor text. And it can be used to create distinctions among otherwise generic Anarchs. It also creates a minor mystery in the sense a vampire who is a member might not be known, and this is something the PCs would need to figure out. It might be fun to speculate who among the original Chicago By Night Anarchs might be a secret member of the Brotherhood. Ironically, the best candidate might be Juggler who clearly would not be a sincere member.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T01:21:18-07:00","id":1486089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1486084#post1486084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since this thread has inspired me to look back at LAbN and develop the Free States for my own chronicles, I've come to certain conclusions on Salvador and his &amp;quot;gang&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Jesus Ramirez is the de facto &amp;quot;baron&amp;quot; of La Hermandad in Los Angeles. He rules the &amp;quot;barony&amp;quot; in Salvador's absence. Many, but not all, of its members come out of the Spanish anarchist tradition. Jesus is one of the major leaders in the Los Angeles Free States. But Salvador Garcia is the leader of &amp;quot;the Brotherhood&amp;quot; which is a North American wide (possibly worldwide) secret society of anarchists among vampires. Members are required to swear an oath to each other as well as to the principles for which the Brotherhood ostensibly stands. (Because secret societies and oaths are cool, and if Salvador was a member of the Mano Negra we should have elements like that in our own new fictional society).<br /> <br /> Unless you are in Los Angeles and in the barony Jesus Ramirez controls, you aren't an actual member of La Hermandad. It's a local factor only. But any Anarch anywhere might be a member of the Brotherhood, which would be a secret society of vampire anarchists. Of course, the barony of La Hermandad would be a place of refuge and indoctrination/training for any member of the Brotherhood, and Jesus would welcome a lot of members of the Brotherhood for a while before eventually kicking them out to go back outside and spread the revolution.<br /> <br /> Technically, there is no distinction between La Hermandad and the Brotherhood. It's just that La Hermandad is a particular local &amp;quot;chapter&amp;quot; of the Brotherhood, and an example of what members of the Brotherhoods in other cities hope to recreate locally.<br /> <br /> In some domains, there may be actual coteries of the Brotherhood where every vampire is a member of the Brotherhood. In other domains, members would belong to coteries whose other members might be other Anarchs or even members of the Camarilla, their membership of the Brotherhood either a secret known only to them or perhaps known to other coterie members depending on the specifics. But they all hold to anarchist ideals and are personally loyal to Salvador Garcia.<br /> <br /> Now, I don't know what it would actually mean to be an anarchist vampire as opposed to what a human anarchist believes. A lot of human anarchism relates to economic issues like the means of production which is totally irrelevant to vampires in regards to other vampires. Maybe some kind of self-governing commune in place of the Prince and Primogen, and no individual domains/hunting grounds with every territory being open to all vampires?<br /> <br /> I think having an actual secret society of anarchist vampires among the Anarchs provides some much needed flavor text. And it can be used to create distinctions among otherwise generic Anarchs. It also creates a minor mystery in the sense a vampire who is a member might not be known, and this is something the PCs would need to figure out. It might be fun to speculate who among the original Chicago By Night Anarchs might be a secret member of the Brotherhood. Ironically, the best candidate might be Juggler who clearly would not be a sincere member.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your idea looks really cool and I think I will copy it. Actually, I think New Orleans bN mentioned a secret society of Anarchs clases The Phoenix Society, and that would be the name I would use, not to make it too obvious.<br /> I still disagree that the main issue in anarchism is the economy. The main issue is freedom and the abolition of hierarchies. Most left anarchists and all anarcho communists oppose capitalism because it generates hierarchies. On the other hand, Agorists, mutualists and anarcho capitalists are anarchist models that support or allow free markets and private property of the means of production.<br /> My point is that vampire Anarchs' goal will be exactly the same: abolition of hierarchies, including both Princes and Bishops, the Camarilla and the Sabbat.<br /> Barons, the way are presented in the books, are a hierarchy and Anarchs shouldn't have them. In my LAbN game the barony system is supposed to be a temporary measure created as a response to the <br /> Sabbat invasiion of 1965, and some of the noted committed Anarchs' are trying to abolish it in 1991. Because they should not be a feature of the system","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T01:57:16-07:00","id":1486090,"title":"","content":"Regarding CbN characters, Anita is the perfect candidate, as she is supposed to have connections all around America","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T08:41:50-07:00","id":1486099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1486089#post1486089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that vampire Anarchs' goal will be exactly the same: abolition of hierarchies, including both Princes and Bishops, the Camarilla and the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't because of what &quot;Anarch&quot; means in the setting.<br /> <br /> While certainly inspired by real Anarchism, in VtM the term refers to anyone that opposes the current sects. That means a lot of those people do not necessarily ascribe to actual Anarchism in any way, shape or form. They may want something more democratic, or a system where the Prince/primogen has to answer to a parliament or to some popular-made laws, or whatever. Most don't have any clear political idea at all.<br /> <br /> Assuming the &quot;Anarch Movement&quot; as something even resembling an actual consistent political movement is silly, which is one reason they always had a problem using the Anarchs. But I do agree that secret societies within the Movement with actual ideologies would be a big improvement.<br /> <br /> For Garcia, I disagree that he would be anti-communist. In the 19th the term was far less defined and frequently used by Anarchists of the time, and Marxists back then wasn't incompatible, in fact Marx himself basically reached Anarchist conclusions through his works in economics. It doesn't mean he would encapsulate every Anarchist thought, but he was be among them. 20th century developments would have a lesser impact on the view of someone that knew 'communism' primarily through 19th century discussion and pamphlets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T10:15:00-07:00","id":1486105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1486099#post1486099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wouldn't because of what &amp;quot;Anarch&amp;quot; means in the setting.<br /> <br /> While certainly inspired by real Anarchism, in VtM the term refers to anyone that opposes the current sects. That means a lot of those people do not necessarily ascribe to actual Anarchism in any way, shape or form. They may want something more democratic, or a system where the Prince/primogen has to answer to a parliament or to some popular-made laws, or whatever. Most don't have any clear political idea at all.<br /> <br /> Assuming the &amp;quot;Anarch Movement&amp;quot; as something even resembling an actual consistent political movement is silly, which is one reason they always had a problem using the Anarchs. But I do agree that secret societies within the Movement with actual ideologies would be a big improvement.<br /> <br /> For Garcia, I disagree that he would be anti-communist. In the 19th the term was far less defined and frequently used by Anarchists of the time, and Marxists back then wasn't incompatible, in fact Marx himself basically reached Anarchist conclusions through his works in economics. It doesn't mean he would encapsulate every Anarchist thought, but he was be among them. 20th century developments would have a lesser impact on the view of someone that knew 'communism' primarily through 19th century discussion and pamphlets.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with introducing parliaments or laws is that vampiric society is very small compared to modern human.societies. When the largest cities have a kindred population similar in size to a small village, representative systems don't make much sense. Hierarchy, direct democracy or anarchy are the most reasonable options. <br /> There is room for reform in the Camarilla, of course, but I wouldn't include the ones who pursue that Anarchs, but Camarilla reformers of progressives. Anarchs should want an abolition of the Camarilla and the Princes' pseudo feudalism and a society based on direct democracy or libertarianism. <br /> Regarding Salvador Garc\u00eda, communist and anarchists actually fought each other during the Spanish Civil War. He doesn't strike me as a theorist, so regardless of what Marx concluded, he would probably have a poor opinion of Marxists, as he would see them as hierarchical and oppressive (specifically in the 1930's under Stalin's leadership)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T15:48:30-07:00","id":1486121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1486105#post1486105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with introducing parliaments or laws is that vampiric society is very small compared to modern human.societies. When the largest cities have a kindred population similar in size to a small village, representative systems don't make much sense. Hierarchy, direct democracy or anarchy are the most reasonable options.<br /> There is room for reform in the Camarilla, of course, but I wouldn't include the ones who pursue that Anarchs, but Camarilla reformers of progressives. Anarchs should want an abolition of the Camarilla and the Princes' pseudo feudalism and a society based on direct democracy or libertarianism.<br /> Regarding Salvador Garc\u00eda, communist and anarchists actually fought each other during the Spanish Civil War. He doesn't strike me as a theorist, so regardless of what Marx concluded, he would probably have a poor opinion of Marxists, as he would see them as hierarchical and oppressive (specifically in the 1930's under Stalin's leadership)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of that, but the question isn't what we think would make sense as a system, it is what different characters would think and the different conclusions they would reach. That's why narrowing it down to one or a few actual ideologies isn't what it actually means to be an Anarch in the setting.<br /> <br /> And a lot of times the &quot;Anarchs&quot; in an arrea are mostly just disgruntled with the Prince, not with the very idea of a Camarilla. They're Anarchs because in practical terms in most domains you're either loyal to the current <i>status quo</i> or you're an Anarch. So I disagree that a reformist would not be considered an Anarch, simply because their society doesn't have the actual space for that distinction (or at least to make it significant).<br /> <br /> Keep in mind what the Anarchs are in most cities in practice: the disgruntled neonates and eventual Ancilla that gather out of the sight of &quot;proper Kindred society&quot; to complain about their ruler and maybe try to coordinate some payback. Or maybe just complain and help each other. Actual philosophies and ideologies may be discussed, but they're secondary to the simple fact those vampires are on the fringes of society but don't want to (or they would be Autarkis)<br /> <br /> That's the general framework, and within it anything goes. People may believe in impossible ideas, or may want to tear down the system, or just make some reforms. They may want a democratic state, or even a theocratic one. Heck, they may want to set an actual monarchy where divine mandate defines the rightful King and see the Prince as an usurper. Everything a normal human can have as an ideology a vampire can have too, but the setting does not have enough political space for all those people to form their own parties and stuff.<br /> <br /> You're either a keeper of the <i>status quo</i> or you're against it, the many reasons and theories behind your position won't change the two options you have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T20:37:26-07:00","id":1486139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1486121#post1486121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware of that, but the question isn't what we think would make sense as a system, it is what different characters would think and the different conclusions they would reach. That's why narrowing it down to one or a few actual ideologies isn't what it actually means to be an Anarch in the setting.<br /> <br /> And a lot of times the &amp;quot;Anarchs&amp;quot; in an arrea are mostly just disgruntled with the Prince, not with the very idea of a Camarilla. They're Anarchs because in practical terms in most domains you're either loyal to the current <i>status quo</i> or you're an Anarch. So I disagree that a reformist would not be considered an Anarch, simply because their society doesn't have the actual space for that distinction (or at least to make it significant).<br /> <br /> Keep in mind what the Anarchs are in most cities in practice: the disgruntled neonates and eventual Ancilla that gather out of the sight of &amp;quot;proper Kindred society&amp;quot; to complain about their ruler and maybe try to coordinate some payback. Or maybe just complain and help each other. Actual philosophies and ideologies may be discussed, but they're secondary to the simple fact those vampires are on the fringes of society but don't want to (or they would be Autarkis)<br /> <br /> That's the general framework, and within it anything goes. People may believe in impossible ideas, or may want to tear down the system, or just make some reforms. They may want a democratic state, or even a theocratic one. Heck, they may want to set an actual monarchy where divine mandate defines the rightful King and see the Prince as an usurper. Everything a normal human can have as an ideology a vampire can have too, but the setting does not have enough political space for all those people to form their own parties and stuff.<br /> <br /> You're either a keeper of the <i>status quo</i> or you're against it, the many reasons and theories behind your position won't change the two options you have.</div> </div> </div> </div>You make great points here. <br /> I think we are looking at the same ideas from different angles. The nuance is even bigger when you have to consider different settings would have different anarch movements.<br /> I am currently running two completely different games in that regard. In my 1991 Chicago+L.A.+Cleveland game the Chicago Anarchs' are a strongly anti hierarchical group, which is partly based on the ideology many of them had before the Embrace. Most of them are Brujah. By their side there are a group of more reformist Kindred, including Maldavis, who are lumped into the Anarch camp not by choice, but because they belong to &quot;low clans&quot;, basically Nosferatu, Gangrel and Caitiff. <br /> And at the same time there are reformists who, by virtue of being Ventrue, Trenere or Toreador, and attending Elysium, are not labeled as Anarchs except in very specific circumstances and only by hard-line conservatives. <br /> In L.A. the situation is different. There we can find a significant group of ideological anarchists, radical democrats or socialiss who are trying to stir Anarch society to a new model of organisation, side by side with a bunch of opportunists who are there just became they had to run away from their Prince's. In Cleveland the Anarchs are lead by a moderate reformist who happen to be a good personal friend of the Prince; obviously, the younger radicals oppose this as cooperation with the status quo.<br /> And in Cairo 2022 anarchists and Anarchs are almost non existent. A group of younger kindred with different reformist agendas gather together under the aegis of an old guard Elder revolutionary Brujah. They don't even call themselves Anarchs, but Modernizers and most of the city Elders leave them be as an inocuous social group","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T10:31:45-07:00","id":1486160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1486139#post1486139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we are looking at the same ideas from different angles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much that, and I like your ideas.<br /> <br /> That was basically my point, from a setting-wide perspective no ideology defines the Anarchs because they're too varied for that. When it comes down to specific places, then we &quot;anything&quot; isn't in the sense that the Anarchs are a formless mass, but that how they look like anywhere else has no bearing on what will the Movement be in this particular place, but <i>here</i> we will have far more specific circumstances.<br /> <br /> In this sense I also agree that secret societies among the Anarchs work really well. They give us a way to have &quot;political parties&quot; within the Movement that will give it color and help delineate ideologies within the constraints of the setting. The Movement in a city is defined by local circumstances, but membership in such a society gives the character a framework of thought through colleagues across the world (given their society doesn't have a strong presence locally), a party line they can uphold or question without feeling alone.<br /> <br /> At the same time, some won't have such a society. And some such societies may be just reformists or something else. With such societies in place I can even picture one actually defending the idea of a parliament, but not just for one Domain...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T10:56:01-07:00","id":1486162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1486090#post1486090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding CbN characters, Anita is the perfect candidate, as she is supposed to have connections all around America</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree heavily. While Anita was certainly an important Anarch, there is nothing in her background that associates her with actual anarchism which would be the point of Salvador's &quot;Brotherhood&quot; (or whatever you want to call it). <br /> <br /> I always imagined her as someone who would have been with the Weather Underground sending out mailbombs to blow up &quot;the pigs&quot; if she had not become a vampire. Those people were radical leftists, but weren't any kind of anarchists. Her biography shows her as someone who was becoming increasingly radical left wing. But she didn't want to eliminate hierarchy, just establish a new hierarchy that would be more &quot;just&quot; according to her political ideology, most of which would require some kind of strong state. She'd be closer to Leninism than anarchism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T12:45:15-07:00","id":1486176,"title":"","content":"One of my other ideas is to go back to one of the stronger NPCs in LAbN which is Louis Fortier. Almost everyone who read LAbN identifies Fortier and his barony as &quot;Camarilla-lite.&quot; His involvement with the Anarch Movement and Free States is almost accidental. He just thought Don Sebastian went too far in his treatment of Jeremy MacNeil, and his sense of justice caused him to side with O'Neil and overthrow Don Sebastian. He then establishes his own domain in west LA / Beverly Hills where he lives with his three blood bond mistresses, like if they were the brides of Dracula, which does not seem like a very Anarchy thing to do. His survival in LA simply seems to be because he sided with MacNeil early on when it truly mattered, and MacNeil protects his mates, as well as a sense of gratitude of the original Anarchs for his help.<br /> <br /> As written though, there's a lot of flaws if we want to make Fortier anything that matters. The first is that his &quot;barony&quot; is just him and his three brides. There's literally no one else per the book. So if we wanted to use his barony as a place where some of the pre-1944 Kindred of the city could have fled to and survive, we need to change canon. But that is relatively easy - expand the borders of his barony a bit and include a few more NPCs. The second is to make him more than just the guy who helped out MacNeil and therefore survived the purge. This is a little bit harder, but I have an idea.<br /> <br /> My model here are the Barons' Wars against the King of England in the 13th century, particularly Simon de Montfort. These were the people behind the Magna Carta and an increased role for parliament. I think this fits well for Fortier whose concern wasn't that there was a Prince, but that the Prince was not constrained in his actions. His ideal form of vampire government would place the Prince in a stricter constitutional role and more enunciated rights for vampires. This would put him on the left wing of traditional Camarilla politics, but certainly no Anarch. His involvement with the Anarchs is an anomaly due to the specifics of the events of 1943-1944.<br /> <br /> So this is how I would run Fortier and use him in the Free States as part of Kindred society.<br /> <br /> First, Fortier and his barony ended up being the protector and haven for some of the moderate Kindred of the Camarilla in LA before the revolt. The Anarchs probably killed most of the existing Kindred, or they fled into exile before they were killed. But some survived and threw themselves under Fortier's protection who prevented them from the Anarch proscriptions. The other Anarchs agreed to this because a) they owed Fortier a lot for his help, and b) those who remained did not have a reputation as lackeys of the elders. (Simply because you want to kill Lodin doesn't mean you think Sir Henry Johnson needs to die.) There's actually characters like that in LAbN already like the Blount Sisters or the Vignes Family, so it's not a stretch. And if we wanted to keep them in their current locations, all we'd need to do is extend Fortier's demand to northern LA like a crescent so it covers Hollywood, San Fernando Valley, Glendale, Burbank, and Pasadena. Most of this area aren't really &quot;baronies&quot; controlled by some warlord anyway, so consolidating them under Fortier won't substantially alter the setting if that is important to you. And we can put any Toreador and other vampires who would be based in Hollywood. In addition to these, I would also give him one or two able lieutenants/supporters who can uphold his reign and protect him and the other Kindred. Best if these were not Ventrue so maybe a Gangrel and Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> None of the Kindred here are really Anarchs, but neither are they politically motivated. The real Anarchs of LA don't really like or trust them, but find them fairly harmless. Justicar Petrodon smartly decided to not set any spies or agents here, though there may be one or two Kindred here he pumps for general information just to keep current. Petrodon knew any agents he recruited here would quickly get exposed so he works in planting them among the real Anarchs instead. Besides, as the right wing of the Anarch Free States, Fortier might one day defect if the Free States deteriorate. Better to bide time than risk alienating a potential future ally.<br /> <br /> Fortier himself runs his barony like a &quot;good prince&quot;. In fact, I'd have him publicly model himself on the Barons Revolts to explain his involvement, and he was the first Kindred leader to be called a &quot;baron&quot;. Eventually MacNeil used the term against all the other Anarch leaders, but whether it was done to remonstrate them for acting like Fortier, or to subtly protect Fortier from accusations he wasn't loyal to the Anarchs is up for debate. The main distinction of Fortier's barony is that 1) he has a list of specific rights that all Kindred enjoy in his domain and 2) restrictions on the arbitrary ruse of his powers, plus 3) a kind of parliament. This is essentially an elected Primogen Council who advises Fortier and brings him any grievances. In truth, Fortier is much less like Simon de Montfort and more like Edward I and his model parliament. Fortier's authority in his barony is absolute for a simple reason, every Kindred there knows he is the only thing that would prevent the actual Anarchs from swarming in, claiming domain, and likely killing most of them. In turn, Fortier is just progressive enough and his friendship with MacNeil and the other original Anarchs of 1944 keeps him as part of the Free States.<br /> <br /> However, every decade that passes sees more of the original 1944 Anarchs destroyed or moved on, and more radical Anarchs arrive from outside the LA area who have no personal connections to Fortier. As such, Fortier's position in the Free States is gradually declining. But MacNeil's support, and his personal rapport with his fellow Ventrue Jesus Ramirez of La Hermandad (and via him, Salvador Garcia) keep him safe. If these pillars of the Anarch Movement and Free States have no problem for him, that is enough for many Anarchs who value a big tent.<br /> <br /> I should also note that Fortier is also a fairly skilled fighter, with Intimidation 5 and having Firearms and Melee at 4. His physical Disciplines are a bit weak. But I would make him sufficiently dangerous that he has destroyed more than one rival/enemy who challenged him. I'd probably add a few more Disciplines and increase his Melee to 5, making him a renown swordsman, perhaps the best on the West Coast. His enemies are frequently staked and decapitated. The other Anarchs respect his physical prowess, and since he never interferes in the internal domains of the other barons, the established Anarch leadership has every reason to leave him alone. It's only newly arrived hotheads who think they can create their own barony at Fortier's expense who get torched. Still for the extreme radicals like Smiling Jack, the time will eventually come when the revolution no longer needs to tolerate Kindred like Louis Fortier, and he'll be lined up on the walls like all the others.<br /> <br /> This ends Part 1. Posting another part to break open the block of text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 07-10-2022, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T12:53:06-07:00","id":1486177,"title":"","content":"Part 2.<br /> <br /> Second, we give Fortier some kind of actual political movement that can go beyond his barony. This would be a kind of Chartism that makes the vampire political system more open and with more guarantees for individual Kindred. It is heavily based on the Conclave system and not only upholds more rights of individual Kindred against the Princes, but the right of domains (i.e. the Princes) against the Inner Circle and the Justicars. The exact nature of these reforms are vague, and change from domain to domain and Kindred to Kindred. The &quot;Chartists&quot; are mostly a movement within the Camarilla, and its advocates spend most of their efforts in conclaves trying to establish precedents and outright controls over certain Princes. We can imagine it was these Kindred who have handled Lodin some of his few defeats in Conclaves near Chicago. But some Chartists adopt insurrectionary movements, particularly against the most despotic of Princes (just like Louis Fortier himself). These rebels would make up the extreme right wing of the Anarchs. But most of the Chartists are at best, &quot;Anarch sympathizers&quot;. But many of these &quot;sympathizers&quot; detest most of the actual Anarchs like Smiling Jack or Salvador Garcia and many others. They favor some variety of Chartism as a reform to prevent the kind of rebellion that overthrow Don Sebastian. They want to prevent the establishment of more &quot;Free States&quot;, and do not share the radical agenda of most Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Fortier himself is a controversial figure among the Camarilla. He is often viewed as a traitor to his kind, and &quot;Fortier&quot; or &quot;Fortierism&quot; is hurled as an insult in Camarilla salons. But Fortier is an elder who was a respected member of the Camarilla and even Primogen when he lived in pre-Sabbat takeover of New York, in San Francisco, and Los Angeles before 1944. He has many friends and maintains ties through correspondence. At time Fortier has even managed to attend some Conclaves and advocated for his position. I like to think that Critias is one of his correspondents, though the Greek philosopher has a poor opinion on Fortier's letter writing style and attempts at political philosophy. He probably thinks Fortier's a bit of a dunderhead, but who isn't when you are Critias? But some respectful comments about Fortier by Critias has given him a good reputation among many Brujah who respect the Greek elder.<br /> <br /> Most Chartists are relatively anodyne and don't threaten the main powers of the Camarilla. Even Fortier himself really doesn't as his ambitions are limited. But some Chartists go much further and espouse abolishing the Inner Circle itself in favor of a &quot;Grand Conclave&quot; who would directly elect the Justicars and supervise them for abuses. Although the current voices calling for this is small, the Inner Circle itself views these Kindred - despite being loyal members of the Camarilla - as more dangerous than actual Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Fortier himself holds no position of leadership among the Chartists. Indeed, he is neither the first Kindred who adopted such a position, nor is he among the leading theoreticians who currently advocate it. He is simply an example, and he does not provide any kind of support to those who act in that philosophy except in encouragement and possible personal friendship.<br /> <br /> Outside of his barony, Chartism holds little appeal among the other Anarchs of the Free States. Though as some Anarchs age, they grow disgusted at the violence and antics of other Anarchs, they may petition Fortier to allow them to become residents of his barony. David Geduld, another Ventrue, does not espouse Chartism, but appreciates Fortier providing a stable right wing of Free State politics. Geduld does not want to be associated strongly with other Ventrue, fearing the loss of his own revolutionary credentials. He tries to model himself on Jeremy MacNeil, but tries to support Fortier how he can out of loyalty to another Ventrue and to prevent the rise of even more radicalism in the Free States.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T17:03:26-07:00","id":1486188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485335#post1485335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Anarchs best work in a Camarilla city as they're basically an essential part of doing what I consider to be a &amp;quot;classic&amp;quot; Vampire: The Masquerade game. The Anarchs serve as one of the factions in a city against the Prince and Elders. They've got their own intrigues, though, and power plays.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is such an important idea that the Sabbat copies it whole cloth, in its Loyalist faction - who chafe against the sect's domination by Tzimisce and Lasombra elders and want to get back to what they see as the Anarch Revolt ideal of &quot;no gods, no masters.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T18:05:31-07:00","id":1486191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1486162#post1486162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree heavily. While Anita was certainly an important Anarch, there is nothing in her background that associates her with actual anarchism which would be the point of Salvador's &amp;quot;Brotherhood&amp;quot; (or whatever you want to call it). <br /> <br /> I always imagined her as someone who would have been with the Weather Underground sending out mailbombs to blow up &amp;quot;the pigs&amp;quot; if she had not become a vampire. Those people were radical leftists, but weren't any kind of anarchists. Her biography shows her as someone who was becoming increasingly radical left wing. But she didn't want to eliminate hierarchy, just establish a new hierarchy that would be more &amp;quot;just&amp;quot; according to her political ideology, most of which would require some kind of strong state. She'd be closer to Leninism than anarchism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely, you have a great point. On the other hand, I can imagine Anita as proponent of the non Hierarchal but strong community systems, similar to Spanish anarcho communism. If you want someone who is fully anarcho communist in CbN that would be Dickie Fulcher, but I don't see him as a member of a secret society","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T20:20:03-07:00","id":1486198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1486191#post1486191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want someone who is fully anarcho communist in CbN that would be Dickie Fulcher, but I don't see him as a member of a secret society</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider Dickie Fulcher just to be another delinquent thug with no aspirations other than it's fun to give the finger to the Man and get revenge on the people who killed his sire/lover. He was a troubled kid who was embraced at the age of 15 by another vampire who was 14, probably because she thought Dickie would be a good boyfriend as she thought he was cute and both liked punk music. This was not a guy who had any real ideas about political philosophy. He's a soccer hooligan without the soccer.<br /> <br /> He insufficiently cared about anything that he wasn't even a member of Juggler's Anarchs. He was one of the &quot;nihilists&quot; coterie whose objective real purpose was to ignore any rules that &quot;annoyed&quot; them.<br /> <br /> Now granted, it's now been over 40 years since his embrace (as opposed to the 15 or so when CbN was first introduced), and I have no idea how he might be portrayed in V20 or V5. But as originally written, this is not a guy who is any kind of deep thinker. He just has a Rebel nature, but is also quite easily lead as long as its towards the things he already wants to do. I would think if he has any real actual beliefs about politics, it's because he is repeating the things he's heard by the people around him, probably some figure that fills the emotional void left by his sire's destruction. Change out that person, and his views would change. In fact, given his friend Damien is now the Sheriff of Chicago in V5, I could just as easily see him helping his old buddy as a lackey just as much as staying with the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> To be honest, if he is still around I'd be shocked. As written, this was not a character that seemed destined for anything other than destruction in a few years. At best, this guy is the kind of cannon fodder Anarch leaders send to their deaths as acceptable losses. &quot;To bad we lost Dickie on that failed attack on the Prince. But we almost got him! Any way, on the next thing...&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T22:43:36-07:00","id":1486204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1485388#post1485388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is because Anarchs are related to the Anarchy as a British period (meaning &quot;without rule&quot;) of history and predates anarchism (small a) as a philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this etymology for &quot;Anarch&quot; ever given within a published book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T22:51:09-07:00","id":1486205,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'm going to be obnoxiously self-indulgent here but discussing Chicago by Night characters IS MY JAM. This is like putting an unknown spellbook in front of a Tremere or your special blood type in front of a Ventrue.<br /> <br /> <b>Dickie Fulcher</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I consider Dickie Fulcher just to be another delinquent thug with no aspirations other than it's fun to give the finger to the Man and get revenge on the people who killed his sire/lover. He was a troubled kid who was embraced at the age of 15 by another vampire who was 14, probably because she thought Dickie would be a good boyfriend as she thought he was cute and both liked punk music. This was not a guy who had any real ideas about political philosophy. He's a soccer hooligan without the soccer. </div> </div> </div>Dickie is actually an interesting case of &quot;read between the lines&quot; from CbN1 to CBN2. The thing about Dickie is threefold:<br /> <br /> 1. He is not a leader but he KNOWS that.<br /> 2. Dickie is actually a monster.<br /> 3. Dickie is best friends with a vampire saint.<br /> <br /> The story of Dickie Fulcher is that he's a Caitiff Anarch punk in the most authentic 1970s punk way that found Maldavis, taught her the ways of the Force, and proceeded to be exceeded by her in every way. He is someone who is fantastically loyal to her because he knows she's smarter, more charismatic, and just plain &quot;better&quot; than him. In the mortal world, Maldavis might have been a Kamala Harris or AOC or killed because it's the World of Darkness. Dickie is waiting for her to get her groove back and save the world.<br /> <br /> Except, there's the slight issue Dickie is a serial killer. He has Humanity 4 but it's probably dropping well past that because he shows up at suburban homes, murders everyone inside, and then stays there until presumably the bodies stink or someone notices. He's destined for wightdom but that's only if Maldavis doesn't find out that her strongest supporter is a mass murderer of middle class surbuban WASPS.<br /> <br /> That was an easy story hook if you were an Anarch. &quot;Do you tell Maldavis her best friend is a monster or handle it yourself? Do you care?&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Anita Wainwright</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I disagree heavily. While Anita was certainly an important Anarch, there is nothing in her background that associates her with actual anarchism which would be the point of Salvador's &amp;quot;Brotherhood&amp;quot; (or whatever you want to call it).<br /> <br /> I always imagined her as someone who would have been with the Weather Underground sending out mailbombs to blow up &amp;quot;the pigs&amp;quot; if she had not become a vampire. Those people were radical leftists, but weren't any kind of anarchists. Her biography shows her as someone who was becoming increasingly radical left wing. But she didn't want to eliminate hierarchy, just establish a new hierarchy that would be more &amp;quot;just&amp;quot; according to her political ideology, most of which would require some kind of strong state. She'd be closer to Leninism than anarchism. </div> </div> </div>Well the thing is we don't actually have to think about what Anita's politics are as she's ideologically a committed Black Panther member. It's interesting how her politics have aged as that organization, so villified by Nixon and the FBI, has been re-examined in light of being less radical in many places and more radical in others. The fact Anita is a white woman is one of those funny &quot;jokes&quot; that you could bring up in game. Not just because, again, Anita being white while her biggest rival (Maldavis) is a black woman but also because the Black Panther Party has a great deal of traditionalist gender views.<br /> <br /> In my write-up of Evelyn Stephens for LET THE STREETS RUN RED, I actually stated that Evelyn Stephens kind of despised Anita for this and this was why the Gary Anarchs didn't ally with the Anarch Center.<br /> <br /> But one of the things I liked about C5 is that Anita is a High Humanity vampire that has the Brujah love of violence and hatred of authority that COULD have made her more radical but resulted in her ending up becoming the Den Mother to the Anarchs of Chicago. She's stepped up and become the kind of Anarch leader they SHOULD be and most want. A leader who looks after their needs, beats down the worst elements, and behaves as first among equals as opposed to a tyrant king. She's probably about the best Anarch leader you could get right now but she's not flawless. For one, she's completely misread Critias and he's likely to knock her head off if she ever gets him alone.<br /> <br /> Likewise, she burns with jealousy over Maldavis who is still a legend even if she's becoming increasingly more like Modius (a useless has been) than turning things around.<br /> <br /> <b>Gengis</b><br /> <br /> I feel the need to bring up Gengis because C5 is pretty much perfect for showing the various trajectories of how the Anarch functions in V:TM society.<br /> <br /> 1. Anita Wainwright illustrates vampires who rise to the occassion of being rabel rousing leaders and heroes (of the Greek sort). Your Salvador Garcias, Jeremy MacNeils, and the Nines Rodriguez.<br /> <br /> 2. Maldavis and Modius (remember he was an Anarch) end up becoming broken by failures and revolutions before retreating into their own little worlds.<br /> <br /> 3. Damien, Sheriff, and Cecily Bain illustrate the Anarchs who just finally say &quot;Fuck It&quot; and join the Camarilla to become what they most despise.<br /> <br /> 4. Juggler, Callahan, Torque, and Gengis illustrate another part of Anarch vs. Camarilla society, which is, <b>The Anarch Moderate</b> or <b>Anarch Puppet</b>.<br /> Basically, there's a decent argument that some Anarch Barons and leadership exist as a double bind layer to the Camarilla's control. Juggler secretly answers to Tyler who is a Primogen member of the group. Gengis answers to Kevin Jackson who showers him with praise and resources while treating him as a peer if not an equal.<br /> <br /> A lot of Anarchs in a city will be nothing more than another tool for the Elders to keep the Anarchs under their thumb. They will get pointed at their enemies and also just harmless acts of defiance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-11-2022, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T13:53:35-07:00","id":1486308,"title":"","content":"Before I move on, I want to note some things that had not occurred to me before. Not about Anarch domains as such, but more details on some characters important to the Free States.<br /> <br /> We know Jeremy MacNeil fled to the Colonies in the late 18th century and participated in events during the American War of Independence. Louis Fortier would have been in New York City during this time as well. It's highly likely these two vampires knew of each other and perhaps even met before LA. It might explain why Fortier defended MacNeil before Don Sebastian and why he was willing to join MacNeil in an attack alongside the Anarchs. Was this truly just noblesse oblige? Or was this done because at one point they were friends during the American Revolution?<br /> <br /> Another possible reason for the two to know each other is that this was the time when the Sabbat was losing their &quot;control&quot; of North America to the Camarilla. They were in civil war, and the Sabbat was already incredibly deranged and becoming increasingly centralized- far removed from their role as Anarchs. It's possible these two might have cooperated in struggles against the Sabbat that cleared the way for more Kindred to arrive, or at least heard of each other's reputation as a result. Having some earlier tie - in any way - I think would have strengthened their relationship and explain why Fortier helped MacNeil and why MacNeil continues to support him. Plus... well the Scots and French are old allies, aren't they?<br /> <br /> It's also highly likely that MacNeil would have met the newly embraced Crispus Attucks at this time (as well as his sire, Marguerite Foccart who was also a neonate at the time) Marguerite's sire was Robin Leeland who is associated with northern England. It's highly likely Crispus knew Robin during his time as a Highland rebel. He might have served as a protector to Leeland's childe and her childe out of respect or paying back a favor he owed. Attucks' relationship with MacNeil might be very old and could very well have extended to Fortier. It makes sense that a natural rebel like MacNeil would arrive in Boston during this time as that city was the hotbed of discontent with the British.<br /> <br /> It is one of the failings of Dark Colony is that it doesn't mention these specific Brujah or any legacy characters associated with them. Sure, it makes generic mention of Brujah in Boston, but all three of these characters had already been detailed in Clanbook: Brujah published the year before. The authors' decision to place the crux of the book a &quot;British invasion&quot; in the late 19th century instead of the earlier colonial era with some established lore seems even more of a mistake now.<br /> <br /> I also find it a bit disappointing that Montreal By Night, published much later, did not make use of Fortier. Its new character of Ventrue Kyle Strathcona, formerly of the Camarilla and later joining the Sabbat, was not somehow tied to Louis Fortier. Per canon, there cannot be any relationship between the 8th generation Strathcona who did not arrive in New World until around 1760 after the French and Indian War (the Seven Years War to you non-Americans), and the 9th generation Louis Fortier (embraced in 1754 by a mysterious female Indian called Night Star). How many Ventrue could possibly be in New France in the colonial period? Having independent Ventrue bloodlines in French Canada this early was a mistake IMHO. It was a big mistake to not tie these characters together somehow. Maybe Strathcona could have arrived in the New World earlier and embraced Night Star, who in turn embraced Fortier? It's not necessary, but it seems like a lost opportunity to me. I'm actually not a big fan making connections to existing characters just to do so, but I do like connections/lineage that make sense. (In any case, Fortier would have never known his sire or her sire, as he was abandoned immediately after embrace.) An Indian vampire at this point of time is most likely, but not necessarily, of the Sabbat line. The Sabbat arrived first and embraced the first Indians. So regardless of Fortier's exact lineage, it means most likely Fortier is of the line of the Ventrue anti-tribu (unbeknownst to him or anyone else). Not actually relevant to a discussion on his character, but I find it interesting.<br /> <br /> What is even more interesting is that Strathcona was written as one of the few Scottish Ventrue, embraced in 1514 and fairly isolated among the Toreador in Edinburgh. This means that Strathcona was also present in Scotland around the time of MacNeil's embrace and living as a Highland rebel, hating the Ventrue. These characters MUST know each other. And they should have a personal history together, likely as each other's antagonists. Furthermore, Strathcona would have left for the New World BEFORE MacNeil. Strathcona would become Prince of Montreal in 1760. MacNeil seems to have arrived during a period of colonial agitation that only began after French Canada became British. Did this have anything to do with MacNeil's decision? Strathcona did not publicly become Sabbat and turn over Montreal to the Sabbat until 1839 or so. Knowing the character of MacNeil, these two should have clashed at some point even if MacNeil never actually visited Montreal while it was ruled by the Camarilla. And since Fortier was in New York at this time as a loyal member of the Camarilla, he would have seen Strathcona as his enemy after this time even if he did not before. We don't know about MacNeil's presence around the 1840s, but I find it interesting that MacNeil and Fortier likely have an enemy in common. And MacNeil being a personal enemy of a Sabbat Cardinal is an interesting aspect of his character. (If you compare their stats, I think MacNeil has the edge.)<br /> <br /> This would also push MacNeil's reputation even further as an enemy of both the Sabbat and Camarilla, and well before the Sabbat's failed attack on the Free States. Specifics like this make him a more compelling character than the rather generic information we've been given.<br /> <br /> Of course, none of this is intentional. It's not mentioned in anyone's biography. They were written independently with likely no thought about the implications. But it makes complete sense if you take each character's biography seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T14:43:40-07:00","id":1486309,"title":"","content":"\u200b\u200bAs part of my pillaging and reinterpretation of LAbN for creating my own version of the Free States in my chronicles, I am on to the next thing.<br /> <br /> I've already covered the personal philosophy of Jeremy MacNeil, making La Hermandad/<b>the Brotherhood</b> an actual anarchist secret society, and the &quot;<b>Chartist</b>&quot; movement that Louis Fortier belongs to. Now I'm moving on to Smiling Jack.<br /> <br /> He's an important Anarch. He was a former pirate in the Caribbean. He participated in the final stages of the revolt of Los Angeles. And he has a greater reputation among the Anarchs than even Jeremy MacNeil, &quot;the Liberator.&quot; While MacNeil has a Rebel nature, that is only Smiling Jack's demeanor. His nature is &quot;Bravo&quot; - meaning he is a bully at heart who torments those weaker than him. Smiling Jack was never a pirate captain per canon, just a second mate. And he has less intelligence and less leadership than MacNeil, but equal to him in charisma and almost as good at manipulation.<br /> <br /> I see Jack as mainly someone who likes to fight, and he's probably done it more than MacNeil. This is a guy who likes to pick fights, and is quite good at it. He's not a coward, but prefers to fight people much weaker than him. Which means most of his fights with the Camarilla is probably at far smaller cities. While he did participate in the revolt in LA, we're told he arrived &quot;during the last bloody stages&quot; meaning when the battle was almost over. I don't see him as someone choosing to fight unless the odds are in his favor. He likely was never in Chicago during Lodin's purge, or if he was he left quickly.<br /> <br /> We know he travels on a big motorcycle and dresses like a biker. I imagine he and whatever crew he hangs out is basically a motorcycle gang. That reminds me of the Wolfpack in Chicago By Night, the coterie of the Archon Tyrus. I imagine one of Tyrus's responsibilities is to patrol the Midwest looking for Jack, and help the smaller Camarilla domains get rid of him should he show up. They are also near contemporaries of one another in terms of physical age and embrace dates. Tyrus has better stats in general, but like all the &quot;authority&quot; figures in CbN have weaker Disciplines than expected (which I think was a design choice). Tyrus interestingly has Bravo as his demeanor, but a nature as Director. I imagine these two and their vampire biker gangs have fought before, but it's mostly been chases and narrow escapes.<br /> <br /> I think Smiling Jack has one main advantage that cements his reputation among the Anarchs. Unlike most of them, he actually lived in a state similar to what many Anarchs would want, or at least idealize. And that is the so-called pirate republics of the 17th century. Smiling Jack would have been a member of the &quot;brethren of the coast&quot; and operated under some kind of articles of agreement. He and his shipmates would have written up their own code of conduct, establishing rules for discipline, division of treasure, leadership, compensation for injury, and so on. All members would have signed the articles and swore an oath to each other.<br /> <br /> I think that is a system that would have a lot of appeal among many Anarchs. Not all of course, but many would like its egalitarian principles, relative simplicity, voluntary compliance, flexibility, and effective means of dispute resolution and punishment. I think this would be the means he would use with whatever crew he is currently riding it, and it is what he would apply to any short lived Free State he might have created in the Caribbean or North America.<br /> <br /> Smiling Jack doesn't need to be any kind of political theorist. He just needs to apply things he already knows about and is used to. Furthermore, such an arrangement doesn't mean the Anarchs have any kind of centralized leadership. Every single Anarch domain or group just needs to have their own articles. Different groups of Anarchs would just learn to live among each other like different pirate crews did in the haven. The &quot;Pirate Republic&quot; in Nassau provides the best model for us. In so far they need some to deal out justice, the different crews (let's not call them gangs) will hammer out another set of articles and elect someone as Magistrate to keep order and dispense justice. If someone doesn't like things, they can leave.<br /> <br /> When Smiling Jack and his crew are in the LA Free States, they treat it similarly like pirates did in Port Royal, Jamaica. They stay for so long and then head back out to loot and plunder. Smiling Jack would probably like it if one of the Free States was modeled this system, but he lives with what he has. But he operates under his own articles, and this is what he probably teaches to a lot of Anarchs as the way to go. He's not actually opposed to other systems - provided they are not forced on him. The more intellectual Anarchs probably disrespect such a simple philosophy, and the physically weaker Anarchs fear the bullying of those who buy into it, but Smiling Jack doesn't care about them. He attracts physically strong vampires who want to do what they want, and like the relatively simple and effective organization it has.<br /> <br /> Jack would hate Fortier, and he probably dislikes the political purist bent and manifestos of Salvador Garcia and his gang of anarchists. He'd see Mohammed (or some other ganglord like him) as a threat, but would respect him as a strong leader and fighter. He should see MacNeil as a personal rival, but probably likes him the best. Too idealistic to be sure, but he likes MacNeil's reputation as a proven fighter and that he doesn't see to push his politics on anyone else. The &quot;MacNeil Boys&quot; might be a touch snobby, but they can be trusted. I imagine when his crew stays in LA, he camps out on MacNeil's grounds, not that of other people.<br /> <br /> We'll call this movement within the Anarchs &quot;<b>the Free Brethren</b>&quot;. The different crews who operate under this system, with their own articles of agreement, likely come up with colorful names for their crews like the pirates of old.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T23:26:51-07:00","id":1486326,"title":"","content":"Let's talk about Mohammed and the Crypt's Sons.<br /> <br /> I am going to keep my comments on this post mainly about how other Anarchs view him and mostly ignore that he is a Sabbat infiltrator, though that may make another post. I'll just say that I actually don't think most of his gang is actually Sabbat. Sabbat members would be limited to just him and whatever childer he may have made. Most of his gang are likely non-Sabbat. Though by the time LAbN was published, he had about 30 years there, I don't think he could simply spam childer and raise them Sabbat. Indoctrination takes some time, and that is VERY risky when you are undercover. He also can't risk converting Anarchs to Sabbat because if he misjudges the situation, his cover is blown. I'm sure by hook or crook, he's managed to get 5 or so Sabbat from his gang of 25. But the rest are probably typical Anarchs destined to be early canon fodder when he makes his move, but before the Sabbat actually invade. He'll make sure they'll get killed while killing other Anarchs while his real pack is kept safe.<br /> <br /> Another question I need to address is what clan does he pretend to be. As far as I can read, LAbN never states it. We know he first helped the Brujah wipe out his old war party, and that is a strong option. Probably better to appear Brujah than be a Caitiff. And since Mohammed &quot;Of the Darkness&quot; is just a little bit too cute for a Lasombra, I think it's better if he's actually known as Mohammed X in LA.<br /> <br /> Many think the gang's name and its association with a real human gang is in poor taste, and I agree. But it can easily be made into a fictitious gang and divested of anything an ST finds problematic.<br /> <br /> So what does it offer us? Well, his best role is what it appears to be - a group representing that element of the Anarchs which comprises real criminals: killers, diablerists, thieves, and other scum that fill up a lot of the Anarch ranks. In other domains controlled by the Camarilla where the Anarchs are a minority, such Kindred may represent a necessary concession to the ranks. If you are on the Prince's hit list, you can't complain about your allies. But LA is different, and Mohammed's gang is an embarrassment to most of the other Anarchs. They'd get rid of him except they waited too long and now they can't. There is just too many of them, Mohammed is too good a leader, and they're dangerous. It'd be a very destructive war. So everyone is hoping Mohammed is actually more reasonable than they fear.<br /> <br /> Now Smiling Jack is also a thug and criminal. But I feel Smiling Jack is legitimately attracted to the free life that piracy once represented to him. Mohammed isn't in it for freedom. He's in this for power. Everyone understands that.<br /> <br /> I imagine Mohammed started relatively small. Maybe with just the coterie he fell into in 1965. But his skills and ruthlessness enabled him to take over or wipe out local rivals until he dominated South Central LA.<br /> <br /> Most of the vampires in LA are young, and neonates tend to carry their mortal lives with them. So there is a racial element. In a city whose Anarch vampire movers and shakers are mostly white or Hispanic, he's really the only major vampire leader who is black. So much of his support are black vampires regardless of their clan - Gangrel, Malkavian, Toreador, whatever. They feel more comfortable with him. Another source are the criminal scum who come fleeing to LA. They won't be welcomed elsewhere, and some can find a home with Mohammed provided they can be of use to him. If Gordon Keaton from Chicago fled to LA, I'm sure he could probably be useful to Mohammed even though he doesn't fit the normal profile as a white yuppie. Of course Gordon couldn't pretend to be a member of the mortal gangs that Mohammed controls. But he doesn't need to be. He can be useful in other areas while supporting Mohammed as vampire warlord of South Central. In fact, he could be very useful precisely because he brings skills and connections Mohammed otherwise wouldn't have. Other examples of CbN NPCs that could fit as part of Mohammed's group would be Dickie Fulcher and Gengis (although Gengis as a natural follower could be justified to appear in most other camps - it all depends on who got to him first).<br /> <br /> An Anarch criminal or gang lord is a perfectly fine concept. There's no reason why it shouldn't be represented in LA. Even though it means Mohammed and his gang really doesn't offer the Anarch Movement any real model to replace the Camarilla unlike the other LA factions. He's just a feature of the local LA Free State scene. Everyone know he's just a powerful gang lord. Feared and respected in southern California, but meaningless to the movement as a whole. And Mohammed is fine with that. Why? Because he's the Duke of LA. He's A #1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TlXHCykk7fU\" data-code=\"TlXHCykk7fU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/TlXHCykk7fU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Now he can provide something useful to the Anarchs. He controls an actual gang that is expanding from its base in LA. Camarilla vampires extend their influence in mortal organizations all the time, so there's no reason why an Anarch can't. As the mortal gang connected to him spreads to other cities, it provides a means for the LA Anarchs to smuggle contraband or Anarchs to other cities. They just need to pay Mohammed for it. Now this is compromised somewhat by the fact that everyone knows this. When the local Camarilla hears that this gang is now operating in their city, they know what it means. But it's still useful. If you are an Anarch in another city that has this gang in it, and you need help, you might be able to utilize it for a price if you know the right people.<br /> <br /> Mohammed has no real allies among the other Anarchs in LA. Any he once had are now either dead or coopted. While he acts nice to most of the other Anarch leaders in the Free States, they are on to his divide and conquer scheme now. Everyone knows that if Jeremy MacNeil wasn't there, that Mohammed would be the most likely candidate to be the &quot;Prince&quot; of LA. He's ambitious to spread his domain further because that is what a warlord needs to do to reward his men. If his &quot;gang&quot; - and his followers should really be the only actual gang in LA in my opinion - is to expand its members, he needs new feeding territories. Everyone knows that the territory of La Hermandad makes the most sense. Jesus Ramirez is doing his best to prepare, but he'll need help. Thankfully he does have allies in LA. And there is a very real threat that Salvador Garcia could mobilize the other members of the Brotherhood in other cities to move to LA as reinforcements.<br /> <br /> So there's nothing special about Mohammed for the Anarch movement as a whole. But he's good local flavor in LA. An example of how the Anarchs can go really wrong. He and his gang can provide a lot to the setting of the Free States even without the secret ties to the Sabbat. If he didn't exist, I think he would need to be invented.<br /> <br /> Edit: OK, I'm going to rule in my chronicles that Mohammed is popularly known as the &quot;Duke&quot; (compare to Fortier being known as the Baron) and colloquially called &quot;A # 1&quot; ever since the movie Escape from New York came out in 1981.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 07-14-2022, 04:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T06:45:25-07:00","id":1486339,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> just straight up killing it in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T21:07:16-07:00","id":1486384,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1190_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1190\" data-vbnamecard=\"1190\">Elphilm</a> Thanks for the kind words.<br /> <br /> In terms of inspirations for the Anarch movement as a whole, I think that is it for LAbN. Everything else in the book is more like &quot;local flavor&quot;. It might add something to the <i>Free States</i>, but doesn't add anything for <i>Anarch</i>s elsewhere. That isn't a bad thing. It's fine. There should be unique things about the Free States that don't matter elsewhere just as there should be other Anarch groups and activities that don't affect Southern California. I'll probably post something in the future looking at the Anarchs in Chicago By Night to see what we can grab, as the Anarchs there are different from those in LA. So a comparison would be interesting, and we might find some interesting inspirations.<br /> <br /> But I'll be keeping my comments to LAbN for now to analyze some of its local flavor, mostly the less powerful local barons. In general, my pronouncement is it isn't very good. More than the characters being bland or indistinguishable from one another (though that too is a problem), the major problem is the book never addresses WHY anyone would follow any of these barons, or WHO exactly make up their followers.<br /> <br /> I'll start with Steve &quot;The Main Man&quot; Booth and David Geduld. These two characters are linked so it's good to discuss them together. First, I have to say that I like both of them as <i>characters</i>. A charismatic vampire surfer dude is perfectly OK. Steve could be a fun andn interesting character for PCs to interact with. And the comparison of his gang to vampires of the movie, The Lost Boys, quickly establishes what kind of vampires they are. Geduld has an interesting enough backstory that he's intriguing. I just don't like them as major <i>barons</i>. And they are major - the author explicitly lists them both as one of the large gangs alongside La Hermandad, the Crypt's Sons, and the baron of San Diego (Tara). But I don't understand who exactly would follow either of these two, or why they'd be able to recruit so many Anarchs (each is around the same size as La Hermandad) as the Free States are described. This is a big failing.<br /> <br /> I can easily imagine Steve Booth as the leader of a <i>coterie</i> around him, most likely his old surfing friends and their girlfriends from the 1960s. Steve's embrace date is 1965 which is the same year of the Sabbat attack that destroyed more than half of the Anarch population. I imagine he was embraced to be a &quot;replacement&quot; for the numbers the Anarchs lost. He's called a &quot;natural leader&quot;, but my impression is more that he is very charismatic, very physically attractive, very chill, naturally likable, and to your bullshit. People like him and want to hang out with him. But he obviously is not a leader. He has no goals, ambitions, or any insight into politics. He just wants to surf and have fun. If I would ever roleplay this NPC, I'd try to do it as a combination of Kiefer Sutherland's David in The Lost Boys and Jeff Bridges' Dude from The Big Lebowski, but with a lot more Beach Boys music. But I don't see him as a <i>baron</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eNqLoFHJxM0\" data-code=\"eNqLoFHJxM0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/eNqLoFHJxM0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I would keep him as a vampire with a small coterie (maybe 3-6 members, heavily utilizing the dynamics of the vampires in The Lost Boys) with limited involvement in the politics of the Free States. The coterie would have &quot;turf&quot; that do protect. But it'd be small and no barony. Just a normal coterie turf. Instead, they'd ultimately rely on a larger protector, most likely Jeremy MacNeil, but it could be another baron. Steve is another childe of Marguerite Foccart, the sire of Crispus Attucks. I think Jeremy and Crispus would look out for him while shaking their head that all this guy wants to do is surf under the moonlight.<br /> <br /> He's good local flavor, but some one who could easily be a one note character if people forget the inspirations.<br /> <br /> Edit: Yeah, I may just move them from Long Beach to Malibu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 07-14-2022, 03:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T21:09:49-07:00","id":1486385,"title":"","content":"David Geduld on the other hand is a natural leader. He's smart, ambitious, and organized. He made partner at a prestigious Chicago law firm (I assume because it is the law form originally created by Lawrence Ballard and thus part of Horatio Ballard's power base) while still in his twenties, and was selected as an agent to infiltrate the Free States as himself under a cover story. Lodin and Ballard would not have selected David for this unless he was highly capable. The cover story must have worked as David, despite know for being a Ventrue of Lodin's brood, was not killed. I assume as part of his defection he provided a lot of accurate (but incomplete or unimportant) information about Lodin's Chicago that would come in useful for the upcoming Anarch revolt there in 1968 along with a lot of misinformation. But he converted to the Anarch cause because the Free States were working (this was in 1963-1965 before the Sabbat attack, so we could assume the Free States were very different back then than how it was in 1994), and performed noted acts of heroism that established his reputation. Basically, he went native and is no longer a spy.<br /> <br /> There's a lot to like about this character, especially as he is a Ventrue who is NOT going to betray the Free States (which would be an <i>obvious</i> and thus <i>boring</i> plot). The problem is determining WHO is following him and WHY? What is his appeal to other Anarchs? What distinguishes him from other barons? We have nothing to go on. We have no example of someone who is a member of his &quot;gang&quot;. We're not given any reason why someone would want to follow him as opposed to someone else. The character may be interesting, but as a baron he's completely bland.<br /> <br /> We're told that when he arrived in 1963 he quickly gathered a small coterie around him. Who was this coterie? Why would established Anarchs in the Free States want to incorporate this guy into their coterie? Or join him if he formed his own coterie? Even with a solid cover story that held up (I imagine Lodin would have called a Blood Hunt on him, and then used his influence with other nearby Princes to do the same, in order to give the cover story credibility), I can't imagine MacNeil, Garcia, or anyone else trusting him. They'd be suspicious for a long, long time. What kind of Anarchs would want to associate with him?<br /> <br /> We could construct reasons for his followers. Maybe he took in those vampires who had lost out in earlier turf wars, and needed a leader. And he created his own childer in the aftermath of the Sabbat invasion. We can create plausible reasons. But in the end, what does this give us? Geduld can't provide any vision for the Anarchs as a whole. He's just a local factor. Nobody in other cities is going to care what he does (though it is amusing to speculate as an Anarch from Chicago, he might be one of Anita Wainwright's contacts).<br /> <br /> But as local flavor, what exactly does Geduld provide the ST in running the Free States? The most obvious thing to do - have him act like a typical Ventrue but who is a loyal Anarch - just makes him even more Camarilla-lite than Louis Fortier. The answer in LAbN, portraying this lawyer as gang leader, is also unsatisfying. Geduld is no street fighter. He has mediocre Firearms and Melee, and no Brawl. This is not a guy who fights with his hands, and most characters likely to be his gang members probably aren't either. The plot set up in LAbN of Geduld leading his &quot;gang&quot; against Steve Booth's surf dudes just seems campy to me once I actually think about it.<br /> <br /> I imagine their fight would go like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8CVQ1KyxLzg\" data-code=\"8CVQ1KyxLzg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/8CVQ1KyxLzg/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Now Geduld could offer a vision of an Anarch domain that actually works - mobilizing influence among mortals, equalizing feeding territory, providing some kind of order, and so on. No theory. Just practicality. But again, this is just Camarilla-lite. Certainly some Anarchs are tired of the violence and constant infighting and may join him. But this would be going over like a lead balloon to most of the population of the Free State. Geduld might be accepted, but he's not highly respected as written. His Status is only 2 compared to MacNeil's 5, Fortier's 3, Garcia's 3, Smiling Jack's 3, and Mohammed's 4. According to the book even Edward Vignes (an old fuddy duddy Ventrue from Pasadena) has Status 3! I interpret this to mean that while Geduld's leadership skills are appreciated, he's not seen as one of the leaders of the Free States. Fortier probably has no problem with him, and MacNeil tolerates him, but Geduld's vision would be rejected by any of the other leaders. Geduld may have talent and ambition, but he's out of place in the Free States.<br /> <br /> Now a Camarilla-lite is OK, but LA already has that in Louis Fortier (or should, as written in the book Fortier's barony is just him and his three brides). It doesn't need another one. Geduld needs something ELSE as a character and faction leader to make him interesting enough to retain.<br /> <br /> I think Geduld works best as the obvious Influence guy in LA. He, like the Toreador Victor Gerard, is the one who helps with the Masquerade. In addition, he's the guy who often handles other threats from the mortal authorities. He makes sure vampires get bailed out, aren't hassled by bureaucrats, and all the other typical Ventrue stuff. He just does it while working with MacNeil. And he is not one of the &quot;MacNeil Boys&quot;, but is someone who makes himself useful to MacNeil and has some credibility as a result. Geduld does have a coterie of his own, and they do live in LA county's South Bay (where Torrance is located). Much of Geduld's direct influence is there. He's not considered one of the &quot;Barons&quot; - that term is associated with the Anarch warlords, but it's acknowledged that South Bay is his territory. He is tolerated as a stabilizing influence in LA. If he has a title or nickname, I imagine it is something like &quot;the Governor&quot;. Something a bit more respectable than baron, but implying less physical power. If his domain needs a name, then something like the South Bay Commonwealth would do. I imagine many Anarchs actually call him the &quot;Prince of South Bay&quot;. But it's somewhat in jest as they acknowledge his loyalty to the Free States.<br /> <br /> Geduld does have followers - vampires who want to be left alone in a fairly safe area - and he obviously must have one or two people who can provide muscle. This is an area where creating additional NPCs is absolutely essential in order to not make him bland. Good place to put a Nosferatu or even Gangrel and balance out all the Brujah. Non-gangsters who would be appropriate for a relatively middle class area. But he'd be easily crushed by any of the larger factions. Mohammed doesn't pay him much attention. Geduld, of course, has higher ambitions. He respects MacNeil, but sees he is not providing effective leadership. He thinks Fortier is too decadent. He probably despises the Anarchs who despise him (but hides it better than they do), but tolerates others. He wants to have more territory, more followers, and more respect. He is just facing the limits of reality in the Free States for one like himself, but Geduld isn't letting that dissuade him. He has all the time in the world.<br /> <br /> I imagine when something important is going down, and the main leaders of the Free States (the Barons) get together to discuss it, they invite Geduld as well. He's too useful, too smart, too organized. If I had to name a role model for him, it'd be him as Alexander Hamilton to MacNeil's George Washington, but without the surrogate son aspect. MacNeil doesn't use Geduld to bolster his own power or domain. He uses Geduld when the Free States collectively needs to get stuff done (particular involving the mortal world) because he's the only one reliable. In a city filled with anarchists, punks, and thugs who don't listen to anyone, Geduld willingly obeys the requests of MacNeil, and it makes him invaluable for that reason alone. He's not MacNeil's prime minister, or his seneschal. His remit isn't to convince the other Anarchs to do things because they wouldn't listen to him. It's to get things done himself using his own resources and those of his coterie on behalf of the Free States. This is a deliberate choice by Geduld. It builds his credibility among the Anarchs, and he also ensures his survival by making himself indispensable. Over time that increases his power. If there is ever another emergency situation like the Sabbat attack in 1965 and MacNeil needed to lead the Anarchs in war, Geduld would promptly return to work as his chief of staff coordinating that army in defense of the Free States.<br /> <br /> Geduld likes the Free States very much (more in 1964 than in 1994 though). Living here is far better than being one of Lodin's brood, constantly doing whatever Lodin wanted immediately done, hemmed in by the Primogen and other powerful elders. Geduld is not an Anarch at heart, but he loves the freedom he has. He loves the freedom it gives him to empire build. He's loyal to the Free States, though <i>not</i> the Anarch movement itself, if that make sense to you. He willing does what MacNeil wants him to because 1) he respects MacNeil personally while acknowledging his weaknesses, 2) someone has to do these things if the Free States are to survive and thrive, and 3) there's no one else. It also helps that the Ventrue Fortier and Ramirez still act like other Ventrue to him, even though there technically isn't a Board. But if they meet from time to time to discuss matters pertinent to the Free States? Well, that's just understandable.<br /> <br /> I think Geduld needs a stronger story that explains his acceptance by the Anarchs, and if you are going with my idea above, why MacNeil uses him. The easiest solution is to provide more details on his heroism during the Sabbat invasion. I think if he collected a group of Anarch survivors who were routed during the initial attack, and then lead them to save MacNeil's life when MacNeil and his boys were ambushed by a Sabbat war party, it would accomplish this. And since Geduld and his &quot;gang&quot; were actually in front of him, MacNeil would naturally send him out to rally the other Anarchs and pass messages. MacNeil would need a fighter like Crispus and his other friends with him. There was no one else to use in this more minor role than Geduld. Geduld did that effectively, and that's when his junior partnership to MacNeil began. Crispus and the others would be on the front lines fighting. Geduld would act as MacNeil's chief of staff and enable him to command an army. That's when MacNeil decided Geduld was someone he could rely on and use.<br /> <br /> When new Anarchs arrive in the city and hear about Geduld and wonder aloud what this Ventrue is doing here, the answer is always the same, &quot;That guy saved MacNeil's life.&quot; That ends most of those conversations.<br /> <br /> While one might think Geduld's and Fortier's &quot;gangs&quot; would be similar, they are very different. Most of the Kindred who dwell in Fortier's barony are old LA types, vampires who were here when Don Sebastian was Prince plus some associates of Fortier who hold his Chartist beliefs. Some others have gone to him seeking protection. In all these cases, Fortier acts as a protective lord. Geduld's group is very different. The Kindred of the South Bay Commonwealth are all Anarchs with similar characteristics. Many were, like his cover story, not Anarchs by choice, but driven to that label because they had angered the local Prince or fled here. Others were idealistic sorts who believed in some generic &quot;freedom&quot; but not beholden to any sort of ideology, but became disillusioned of the violence that characterize the Free States. Geduld recruits the <i>best</i> of these - those whose skills he needs whom he personally likes- to join him in the Commonwealth. To the others he lends a sympathetic ear and occasionally some help, but does not invite to the Commonwealth. They might prove of use if they remain in LA in one of the other baronies (usually MacNeil's). His &quot;gang&quot; is basically a very large coterie who help him build power and influence. There all part of the same &quot;team&quot; that wants to live in the same kind of domain. He likes skilled Kindred who are ambitious, but not too ambitious. He doesn't want anyone who might eventually challenge his leadership. In exchange, he keeps out the criminals, punks, drifters, and riff raff. Geduld avoids performing the same tyranny of the elders simply because the rest of the Free States is his dumping ground. Again using the Anarchs of Chicago By Night as an example, someone like Modius or some of the other Socialists coterie might settle with Fortier. Kindred like Priscilla Biggs, Damien, and Uriah might be in the Commonwealth. Maldavis could also naturally fit here, but it's possible Geduld would not accept her because he feared she might want to take charge. He likely would not accept Hank Cave either, thinking he would not have anything to offer him. Neither Fortier or Geduld would like to see any of the other Chicago Anarchs in their territory.<br /> <br /> Since we're using a Washington/Hamilton analogy, then it would make sense to use Crispus Attucks as the Thomas Jefferson of the three. These guys do not get along. Crispus sees him as too ambitious, someone with his own agenda, not a &quot;true believer&quot;, and above all too... too Ventrue. MacNeil agrees, but reminds his old friend that since Crispus frequently travels so he has to rely on <i>somebody</i>. And Geduld is the most reliable. MacNeil is not friends with Geduld as he is with Crispus. He tolerates him as someone useful. He also acknowledges that Geduld is not a yes man or lackey, but his own man with his own dreams and ambitions. He is not obsequious like Victor Girard. And Geduld is devoted to building his own territory. MacNeil respects that and can work with such a person. That's a good little coterie chart of the three.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qk48HAkbuqk\" data-code=\"qk48HAkbuqk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/qk48HAkbuqk/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Geduld, in many respects, is the guy Victor Girard would want to be. Or at least Victor wants to be whom he <i>thinks</i> Geduld is to MacNeil, which is not actually the case. The difference is that Geduld is both more ambitious - he ultimately sees himself being the leader of Los Angeles - and more loyal. He won't betray MacNeil or tolerate the Camarilla returning, not even if they offered him the position of Prince. Victor wants personal power and the privileges that come with it. Geduld wants to build an empire, a legacy. Those are very different things.<br /> <br /> Thinking about David Geduld was hard. I liked the character's backstory, but could not think of a good way to actually use the character as any kind of Anarch leader. I was tempted to just get rid of him entirely. But I think I figured out a way to keep him, still be true to his core concept, while providing some actual interesting flavor to the Free States.<br /> <br /> Now, on to the other Anarch barons. I won't be as generous in my assessment of those characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 07-14-2022, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T21:23:32-07:00","id":1486492,"title":"","content":"After my stupidly long post on David Geduld, I promise I'll make them shorter.<br /> <br /> The remaining barons in LA proper in LAbN (not counting Free States that are farther away like Tara's in San Diego) are Allison Maller in Anaheim and Amethyst in Santa Clara, right next to each other. Amethyst is fighting a secret war against Allison through a pawn and is hoping that taking over two cities would make her a major baron. Amethyst doing this in secret because if it is found out she's behind it, the other barons would step to prevent another big player as it would destabilize the current status quo.<br /> <br /> There are things I like here. Having at least one baron be female is welcome. That one of them is a Caitiff is even better. The Caitiff is also another racial minority, and that helps ground the setting. But there is a major problem.<br /> <br /> We don't know why any Anarchs would follow either of these characters. Or would prefer one to the other as their leader. Or what separates their groups from each other, or indeed from any of the other gangs. This is essentially the problem with LAbN. The &quot;gangs&quot; are bland and boring. Very different from the Anarch groups in Chicago. But then again, we had coterie charts in CbN that explained the common theme of each group, how its coterie members acted towards each other, and how the different Anarch groups viewed each other. There isn't any of that in LAbN. Nevertheless, the author wants us to think this conflict is a major one that should take up the interests of the PCs. In a latter section he even adds the words (hint, hint) that this is something the ST should steer the PCs to get involved with. But why should they?<br /> <br /> Based on the individual history of the NPC, there was at least something that I could tease out about MacNeil, Fortier, Garcia, Mohammed, and their groups. Steve Booth really didn't fit the profile of a baron, but at least he was distinctive as a character. It was much harder to figure out what I could do with Geduld, but eventually I modified his concept enough that fit the strengths of his interesting character history (at least it's interesting to me).<br /> <br /> But Allison and Amethyst? I don't see why anyone would follow them. Their character description has a common problem with many NPCs in LAbN - we're told things, but not shown them. So while it's mentioned that they recruited followers, or that one is renowned for toughness and not letting anything stop her, we as the reader have no idea WHY.<br /> <br /> What's worst is that these characters essentially share the same core concept. In fact, it's a concept that surprisingly fits several additional NPCs in the book. The core concept is 14-16 year old hot jailbait who uses her sex appeal as a weapon. That's fine as a concept for ONE character. It gets weird when there's more than one.<br /> <br /> How can anyone pick sides if the two characters and their groups are indistinguishable?<br /> <br /> While it's possible one can begin brainstorming ideas and modifying both characters, if you are going to do that why not just create one or more of your own NPCs that will be more distinctive? I bothered with David Geduld because I actually liked his character profile. I just don't find either of these characters that interesting. There's nothing about their character background or non-existent coterie description that could serve the basis of an interesting faction. So it's just more generic Anarchs fighting.<br /> <br /> I'll be leaving my notes blank on this area. If I have future inspiration, I may come back and write up more interesting coteries and their leaders for my chronicles.<br /> <br /> It's too bad because I think the surface level details fine. Having an actual war between two minor factions is good. It demonstrates the decline of the Free States, but won't usurp a chronicle like Mohammed beginning his war. I like that there's two female characters leading their coteries. So far LAbN has neglected them. However, instead of having a bland &quot;baron of Anaheim&quot; and &quot;baron of Santa Clara&quot;, I'd probably just refer to the area as Orange County as a singular entity, and the squabbles be based on some kind of competing visions or interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T21:24:23-07:00","id":1486493,"title":"","content":"The generic and bland characters of LAbN is its big downfall. And the lack of coterie charts hurts too. It was also a bad decision to concentrate the character section exclusively on the &quot;important&quot; NPCs. Around 40 characters are described in the book, but there's over 170 vampires in the LA Free States (not counting outskirt domains like San Diego). 130 extra characters is a lot for an ST to describe. And the blandness of the examples we have does not do much to inspire the ST. Very different from Chicago By Night whose diverse and interesting characters (many with pertinent history in real Chicago events, or with events among the local vampires) can fuel the ST's imagination. And the idea that everyone runs in &quot;gangs&quot; instead of &quot;coteries&quot; likewise limits the imagination. It's not a surprise people want to take the more interesting NPCs in the Bloodlines computer game and put them here. They should.<br /> <br /> I do have my own ideas for new characters that would provide interesting flavor. But all that would be is me saying &quot;Here's my cool new character!&quot; that I either created or borrowed from someone else. That really doesn't add anything, so I'll refrain.<br /> <br /> Next up I'll take a look at CbN and see if we can take anything useful from there for the Anarch Movement as a whole, or perhaps even back to the Free States.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T21:52:22-07:00","id":1486494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them?p=1486493#post1486493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The generic and bland characters of LAbN is its big downfall. And the lack of coterie charts hurts too. It was also a bad decision to concentrate the character section exclusively on the &quot;important&quot; NPCs. Around 40 characters are described in the book, but there's over 170 vampires in the LA Free States (not counting outskirt domains like San Diego). 130 extra characters is a lot for an ST to describe. And the blandness of the examples we have does not do much to inspire the ST. Very different from Chicago By Night whose diverse and interesting characters (many with pertinent history in real Chicago events, or with events among the local vampires) can fuel the ST's imagination. And the idea that everyone runs in &quot;gangs&quot; instead of &quot;coteries&quot; likewise limits the imagination. It's not a surprise people want to take the more interesting NPCs in the Bloodlines computer game and put them here. They should.<br /> <br /> I do have my own ideas for new characters that would provide interesting flavor. But all that would be is me saying &quot;Here's my cool new character!&quot; that I either created or borrowed from someone else. That really doesn't add anything, so I'll refrain.<br /> <br /> Next up I'll take a look at CbN and see if we can take anything useful from there for the Anarch Movement as a whole, or perhaps even back to the Free States.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's also the fact that of all the things to do in LA, it's weird how they laser-focused on gangs.<br /> <br /> Hollywood being all but ignored except for a Bela Lugosi impersonator and a 15 year old Methuselah is pretty damn strange.<br /> <br /> And NO nightclubs in the city that actually DOES have all the nightclubs that V:TM describes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T22:06:32-07:00","id":1486496,"title":"","content":"Yep. I agree with all of that. <br /> <br /> The book makes poor use of its real life setting, but I think most would agree that was the case of all By Night books other than Chicago.<br /> <br /> It also, as I said, leaves out a whole lot of relevant detail. Simply having more characters to flesh out each &quot;gang&quot; and lesser vampires and putting in a coterie chart, would have forced the authors to develop more interesting characters and groups. I get the impression that ultimately the book was too ambitious for its authors. And it needed a higher page count.<br /> <br /> But I was surprised that simply giving some real thought about the characters and their &quot;gangs&quot; that we're told about, can lead to some interesting distinctions. I actually ended up with a lot more useful information for my own setting notes than I expected. But there still needs a lot of work for me to do before my notes turn into something I can use to run an actual chronicle. But I now have a map at least of what I need to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T05:08:26-07:00","id":1486510,"title":"","content":"Poor use of geography is a strength and a weakness.<br /> <br /> Strength: because getting really particular about the history of the city can feel a bit exclusive. Weakness, because geography (well, city planning) really can influence what domains go Anarch or not. American style city planning (not all cities are like this, I more refer to small, super tall downtowns with the rest of the city being endless low-density sprawls of car parks, roads and suburbs) really encourages anarchs because the differences between domain quality is really extreme, and car reliance disfavours elders. In europe, cities are more equal, and this reduces the pressure on vampires, making them less likely to go Anarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T22:34:47-07:00","id":1487110,"title":"","content":"The Anarchs were a major faction in both Chicago By Nights, and many historical events there (the Haymarket Riots and rise of Socialism in the late 19th century, the Nights of Rage and Democratic Convention riots of the late 1960s, and the mayoralty of Harold Washington and the Council Wars of the mid 1980s) involved the Anarchs. Looking back, is there anything the Anarchs there can teach us about Anarch domains or the Anarch Movement in general?<br /> <br /> Chicago By Night 1e has three Anarch factions: the Nihilists, Hind's Socialists, and Juggler's Anarchs. Let's look at each one.<br /> <br /> The Nihilists are a bunch of immature, emotionally stunted ne'er-do-wells, losers, and thugs. Quite typical for a large section of Anarchs. They don't contribute anything to the Anarch movement other than as cannon fodder - provided they can be convinced to join in when it matters. There's probably several coteries of such Anarchs in the Free States, mostly in MacNeil's barony as he's probably the only one who would tolerate them.<br /> <br /> Hind's Socialists are more interesting from a historical perspective. Although described as has-beens in the 1990s, they were the leaders of the Anarchs in the 1890s. Although they can be described as the closest thing to thinks among the Chicago Anarchs, it's important to remember that these are essentially trade unionists. They believe in organizing and mobilizing. They aren't intellectuals. Modius is a member, which I used to think as strange. Modius is a Prince. He couldn't be an Anarch, right? Well, reading both CbN 1e and CbN 2e again I've come to a different conclusion. It's fine for Modius to be both a Prince and an Anarch. In Chicago, this isn't a contradiction. The position of Prince is not seen as inherently tyrannically. It's the person in that position and whether she serves &quot;the Elders&quot; or not. How Anarchs win is by putting one of their own as Prince (who will presumably run the domain more equitably). This becomes very explicit in CbN 2e when we have several Anarchs mentioned as candidates for Prince. It also makes it clear that in this era, the Anarchs really were part of the Camarilla and not any actual separate sect. Individuals among the Camarilla were an enemy, and the Inner Circle and the Justicars part of the elders. But the basic structure of Princes and domains, which is what most players think of as the Camarilla, is equally part of the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Before the establishment of the Free States, I think this was probably quite normal. That makes Jeremy MacNeil's refusal to become the next Prince truly revolutionary, and making him deserve the title of &quot;Liberator&quot;. It\u2019s like Washington not becoming king or retiring after only two terms. It established the Free States as an experimenter of different kinds of alternative governments. I think this is something that is important to point out as an ST, as it makes the Free States seem more attractive, and more revolutionary.<br /> <br /> Going back to Hind's Socialists, I don't see them as something new to the factions already created on this thread. They'd simply be other members among the &quot;Chartists,&quot; although among its more radical members. This would also make Fortier and his domain more acceptable in the Free States of 1944 then it would be in future eras. What he'd be doing would be much more inline with traditional Anarch thought back then.<br /> <br /> Another interesting thing about this group is that they have mainly stopped worrying about Chicago, instead giving much more thought on longer term issues like the Jyhad and Gehenna. I think at the time, this was meant to show them divorced from reality and thinking about boogeymen. But now I think I'd run them much more seriously, giving good thought on how the Anarch Movement can survive in the long term and protect the members of the Movement. I don't know how exactly I'd portray that in game yet, but I would portray them as doing long term thinking, and not just how to seize power in a single domain. Perhaps they'd advocate for the need to expand the Conclave system, and have some sort of Grand Conclave replace the Inner Circle. Maybe even keep the Justicar system (although perhaps renamed), but make it more accountable.<br /> <br /> This post is getting long, so I'll discuss Juggler in a future post.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T23:48:34-07:00","id":1487114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\">